{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghrkd8HaKGAQM4vFgMdr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SH7UB8T5GyGhjPtrVms1ow","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050554__x4cdb93/work/PLAN.md","offset":800,"limit":450},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15530,"cache_read_input_tokens":37615,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15530},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3fa61e8-1431-4900-ae89-edc59162574b","uuid":"a540b62c-a2f4-43a2-be4a-01a95e1dcf38","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:06:09.359Z","request_id":"req_011CghrkcqBYnKPy1erN3XCD","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SH7UB8T5GyGhjPtrVms1ow":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050554__x4cdb93/work/PLAN.md","offset":800,"limit":450}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SH7UB8T5GyGhjPtrVms1ow","type":"tool_result","content":"800\t- Shared camera (director keyframes only), shared animals, first hit takes it; each player has their own rifle, calls,\n801\t  score, stats; benching is per player (benched players watch); the site's end rules (5.7) apply to everyone.\n802\t- The tally shows a column per player; hunt results show a podium; the winner may enter initials.\n803\t- A pad unplugged pauses with the engine's message (per player).\n804\t\n805\t**Tests** (flow/party): two and four scripted players join; each has its own tube and score; a doe benches only its\n806\tshooter; a shared kill splits points; the podium orders players by score.\n807\t\n808\t### 5.12 HUD, prompts and glyphs (`51-hud.js`, `52-glyphs.js`)\n809\t\n810\t10-foot rules: the HUD is sparse and large. At 480 x 270: key numbers at font scale 2 (14 px), banners at scale 3-4,\n811\tcaptions at scale 1 with a shadow in a dark band; 12 px safe margins; clear of `game.cornerArea()` and, on a phone,\n812\t`input.touchArea()`.\n813\t\n814\t- **Top centre**: site name and clock (0:42); under it a row of buck icons (antler silhouettes: hollow = to come,\n815\t  filled in the bagger's colour = bagged, crossed = escaped or lost).\n816\t- **Player panels** (P1 bottom left, P2 bottom right, P3 top left, P4 top right): score, five shell icons with a\n817\t  chamber light, call charges (horn icons), breath arc while scoped, BENCHED tag.\n818\t- **Centre banners**: BUCKS ONLY!, HEART SHOT!, DOE! YOU'RE OUT!, TROPHY!, TIME!, with an extruded `E.font.title`\n819\t  style, 0.9 s, a whoosh.\n820\t- **Score pops** in the world over the animal: \"+425 HEART SHOT 86 m\" in the shooter's colour.\n821\t- **Captions** (barks and dialog) lower centre with the speaker's name and colour.\n822\t- **Prompts** lower centre, contextual (PUMP!, HOLD [L2] TO SCOPE, CALL [△]), shown only when relevant and for a\n823\t  limited number of times per hunt.\n824\t- **Rival tag** (campaign): top left under P3's place: \"DWAYNE 4,600\".\n825\t- **Hold to see standings** (Tab or Create; unbound in hub rounds): a centre table of players' scores.\n826\t\n827\t**Glyphs**: `Prompts.label(action, player)` decides the family by the player's last device: `gamepad` -> the pad's\n828\tglyph (`input.label(action, 'gamepad')` gives '✕', '○', '□', '△', 'R2', 'L2', 'R1', 'L1' with PlayStation symbols, or\n829\t'A', 'B', 'X', 'Y', 'RT', 'LT', 'RB', 'LB' with Xbox); `keyboard` or `mouse` -> one KB+M family: actions bound to a\n830\tmouse button show the mouse icon once the mouse has been used this session, others show the key (R, Q, Shift, Space,\n831\tEsc, Tab, Enter). `52-glyphs.js` draws each as a pixel icon: PS shapes in their colours (blue cross, red circle, pink\n832\tsquare, green triangle) on dark discs, trigger and bumper tabs, stick icons, Options and Create pills; Xbox letters on\n833\tcoloured discs; keycaps (wide for Space, Shift, Enter); a mouse with the left, right or wheel highlighted. The default\n834\tbutton symbols are **PlayStation**; Settings > Controller > Button symbols offers Xbox (engine setting, default changed:\n835\tAppendix C).\n836\t\n837\t**Tests** (unit/prompts): with a pad last used, labels are PlayStation glyphs by default and Xbox letters after\n838\t`settings.set('glyphs', 'xbox')`; with the mouse used, fire shows the left-click icon and pump shows R; every action\n839\tthe HUD prompts has an icon in all three families; every caption and banner fits the screen width at its scale\n840\t(`E.font.width`).\n841\t\n842\t### 5.13 Feedback and juice\n843\t- Shot: a 1-2 px screen shake (comfort setting respected), reticle bloom, gunshot with a valley echo (5.20), a pad\n844\t  rumble (0.35, 0.08 s) for the shooter.\n845\t- Kill: hit-stop 0.04 s (`game.freeze`), callout banner for lethal zones, score pop, the bagged tag; a stronger rumble.\n846\t- Doe: a red-tinted flash (flashes setting respected), the sad-trombone sting, the emcee's groan, the BENCHED reticle.\n847\t- Multi-kills, long shots (150 m and more: LONG SHOT!), running shots: their own barks.\n848\t- **Trophy Cam** (trophy kills, and in single player the last buck of a site if it was a heart shot; setting On /\n849\t  Trophies only / Off): the sim runs at `game.timeScale = 0.15` while the camera flight takes 1.4 s of unscaled time\n850\t  (`game.real`): the lens flies from the vantage along the shot's ray to 3 m from the impact, the fov narrows, a\n851\t  bullet streak leads; at impact the animal flashes to its x-ray look (skeleton, heart and lungs) for 0.35 s; normal\n852\t  speed for its collapse; back to the vantage with a fade; time scale restored. Skippable (confirm). Never during\n853\t  local multiplayer or hub rounds (they show the Shot Chart only). Under Reduce motion it is a still x-ray card.\n854\t- Skunk: a green dithered cloud over 60% of the screen fading over 3 s, a \"pfft\" and a stink chord.\n855\t\n856\t### 5.14 Tally and the Shot Chart (`60-tally.js`)\n857\tA full-screen card over the dimmed, frozen vista, one beat at a time (10-foot friendly), confirm to skip ahead:\n858\t1. SITE CLEAR or TIME!, the site's name.\n859\t2. For each bagged animal, a card: its x-ray side view (`rig.drawXray`: a dithered translucent body, skeleton lines,\n860\t   heart red and lungs pink, entry marks where each round went, labelled HEART / LUNG / GUT...), its distance, antler\n861\t   points or spread, and its points line counted up with ticks.\n862\t3. Critters, penalties, accuracy, clean sweep, no-penalty bonus, site total; the stars (antler icons) pop in.\n863\t4. Party: a column per player, then the site's leader. Campaign: the standings strip against the rivals.\n864\tPrompt: [✕] CONTINUE (per device). Confirm is ignored for the first 0.6 s (Space pumps in play and confirms here, so\n865\ta late pump doesn't skip a card). Auto-advances after 12 s in the attract mode.\n866\t\n867\t### 5.15 Trophy encounters (`61-trophy.js`)\n868\tA trophy site is a site with a legend, one named animal and rules of its own (6.3). Shared parts: a campfire legend\n869\tdialog before it (Uncle Dub), tension music layers in when the trophy is on screen, the trophy shows a TROPHY tag the\n870\tfirst time it's seen, its HUD icon is gold, it has 1.5x the species' hp and ignores the call except where its rules\n871\tsay, and a miss makes it bolt (its window ends). Bagged: Trophy Cam, TROPHY BAGGED!, x3 points, its mount unlocks in\n872\tthe Lodge. Escaped: THE ONE THAT GOT AWAY (no penalty). Saved in records either way (seen, bagged, best distance).\n873\t\n874\t### 5.16 Bonus games (`62-bonus.js`)\n875\tA framework for 30-second shooting galleries on the same landscape at a bonus vantage: a target spawner on a\n876\ttimeline, thrown or flying targets on ballistic arcs (`E.arc`-style maths in world space) or `E.Path`s, the same rifle\n877\trules with a bigger tube and faster rack, per-target points, protected targets with penalties, a PERFECT bonus (every\n878\ttarget hit with no misses doubles the bonus total), and a bonus tally. The three games are in 6.4. Bonus Only mode plays\n879\tany of them from the menu; they keep their own high-score tables.\n880\t\n881\t### 5.17 Modes and menus (`90-title.js`, `91-menu.js`, `92-hunt.js`, `94-about.js`, `53-ui.js`)\n882\t\n883\t**Title**: the logo (`E.font.title`, wood-and-brass gradient with a blaze-orange outline, \"THE 41ST ANNUAL\" above it)\n884\tover a live vista (Hollow Creek at dawn, deer grazing, slow pan); PRESS [START] in the last device's glyph; the\n885\tengine's corner menu button (settings) at top right. CONTINUE appears in the menu when an autosaved Hunt-Off exists.\n886\t\n887\t**Main menu** (big cards, one column, focus with d-pad, stick or arrows; hover with the mouse moves the focus; click or\n888\tconfirm picks; cancel goes back; a prompt bar at the bottom shows confirm and back glyphs):\n889\t\n890\t| Entry | What it does |\n891\t|---|---|\n892\t| HUNT-OFF (or CONTINUE HUNT-OFF) | the campaign: Hollow Creek, Bugle Ridge, Muskeg Lake in order, rivals and standings, ceremony; autosave after each hunt (`game.saves` autosave slot) |\n893\t| SINGLE HUNT | pick one of the three hunts (card with species, time of day, trophy silhouette, best score) |\n894\t| PARTY HUNT | the join page (players press Options or Start on their pads; the mouse player is P1), then pick a hunt or QUICK DRAW (site 1 of each hunt plus Saucer Season, time-boxed; a short loading card raises each landscape between them) |\n895\t| BONUS GAMES | pick Crow Patrol, Saucer Season or Snowball Standoff |\n896\t| PRACTICE RANGE | Uncle Dub's range: the tutorial (6.5) |\n897\t| THE LODGE | the trophy room (5.18) |\n898\t| SETTINGS | the engine's settings screen (`game.menu('settings')`) |\n899\t| ABOUT & CREDITS | 5.27 |\n900\t\n901\t**Difficulty** (picked on the hunt card, remembered): Easy (Strong assist, auto-pump, animals x0.85 speed, +1 call),\n902\tNormal, Pro (no assist, animals x1.15 speed, does mixed in more often, scope sway x1.3).\n903\t\n904\t### 5.18 The Lodge, records and saves (`93-lodge.js`)\n905\t- A cozy side-view room built with the engine's own 2D pipeline: a `side` view, a PlatformMap floor of `wood` tiles and\n906\t  a log back wall (`back` tiles, `plank` material), engine props and shapes (fireplace from custom shape, table, chairs,\n907\t  bench, bookcase, barrel, lamps; `light: true`), warm canvas lighting with a flickering fire, Uncle Dub in a rocking\n908\t  chair (Humanoid, idle; waves when focused), a sleeping hound (Blob).\n909\t- The trophy wall: plaques for Old Iron Rack, The Duke, Big Mo (dark silhouettes until bagged, then `rig.drawMount`),\n910\t  each hunt's best buck, and the records chalkboard (E.Arcade tables per mode with initials, preloaded with DUB, MAE,\n911\t  DWN, LOR, ERL). Focus moves along the wall (d-pad, stick, arrows, mouse hover); the camera pans to it; a big info\n912\t  card shows its story, distance, date bagged.\n913\t- Stats card: hunts played, shots, accuracy, bucks bagged, does shot, longest shot, favourite rifle sound (a joke line).\n914\t- `Records` in `E.store`: best scores per mode and hunt, stars per site, trophies, stats, the Range badge. In AI Hub\n915\t  sessions storage is a throwaway memory store (the client's), so nothing special is needed.\n916\t\n917\t### 5.19 Dialog, barks and voices (`71-barks.js`, `babble.js`)\n918\t- **Dialog** scenes use `E.Dialog` with Humanoid portraits; `voice: null` and our Babble voice plays the line. Story\n919\t  beats are data (`def('beat', ...)`): a list of `[speaker, line]` with optional pose and expression.\n920\t- **Barks**: categories (6.9) with 3-6 lines each; picked without repeating the last two (fx stream); the emcee shouts\n921\t  them as a caption plus a short Babble burst; at most one bark per 1.2 s, high-priority barks (doe, trophy, triple)\n922\t  cut in.\n923\t- **E.Babble** (Animalese/Simlish style): each line becomes syllables (letter pairs; vowels pick the pitch step),\n924\t  12-16 syllables a second, each a 40-70 ms blip through a band-pass \"formant\" filter per vowel; per character: base\n925\t  pitch, waveform, speed, pitch spread, warble. Exclamations rise at the end; questions rise; ALL-CAPS barks are louder\n926\t  and faster. Voices: Emcee (140 Hz square, boomy, echo), Uncle Dub (105 Hz saw with noise grit, slow), Granny Mae (260\n927\t  Hz sine with vibrato), Dwayne (185 Hz 12.5% pulse, nasal), Loretta (225 Hz triangle, bright), Earl (95 Hz square,\n928\t  slow and warm). Uses `game.audio.ctx` and the exposed sfx bus (Appendix C); silent headless.\n929\t\n930\t### 5.20 Audio (`70-audio.js`)\n931\t\n932\t**Music** (engine song notation; bluegrass chiptune):\n933\t\n934\t| Song | Where | Sketch |\n935\t|---|---|---|\n936\t| `hoedown` | title, menus | 140 bpm, G major: pulse-25% banjo rolls in 16ths, square fiddle melody, triangle root-fifth bass, washboard noise and rimshots |\n937\t| `lodgefire` | Lodge, About | 84 bpm, warm square \"harmonica\" with vibrato over triangle chords, soft brushes |\n938\t| `stalk` | hunt sites (layers) | 96 bpm pads and pulse ostinato at low volume; layer `drums` comes in when bucks are on screen, layer `tension` (heartbeat kick, tremolo) when a trophy is on screen (`audio.layer`) |\n939\t| `jamboree` | bonus games | 160 bpm hoedown, fast fiddle |\n940\t| `results` | tallies, hunt results | 110 bpm strut |\n941\t| `fanfare`, `siteclear`, `doe`, `escaped`, `newrecord` | stings (`audio.sting`) | trophy fanfare; clear jingle; sad trombone slide; two-note fall; initials theme |\n942\t\n943\t**Ambience** beds per hunt: wind (filtered noise, slow swells), birdsong chirps (random sine and pulse blips by time of\n944\tday), creek or lake lapping, distant crows (Hollow), elk chirps and distant bugles (Bugle), loon calls and ice creaks\n945\t(Muskeg).\n946\t\n947\t**SFX** (engine voices, lists with `delay` for layering): rifle shot (noise crack 0.05 s high-passed + 60 Hz sine\n948\tthump 0.15 s + low noise tail 0.6 s + two echoes at 0.35 s and 0.8 s, quieter and darker, the echo delay longer across\n949\topen valleys); dry click; pump rack (two band-passed clicks 0.09 s apart with a slide); shell inserts; scope raise\n950\t(cloth swish); breath in and out; calls (grunt: 90 Hz saw wobble; bugle: sine 500 -> 1800 Hz glide with vibrato and\n951\ta noisy scream; moose: 70 Hz saw \"waugh\"); impacts (fur thump, wood knock, rock ricochet whine 3000 -> 1200 Hz,\n952\tdirt thud, splash); hooves by gait; animal voices (snort, cow-elk chirp, turkey gobble trill, duck quack, crow caw,\n953\tsquirrel chatter, marmot whistle, wolf and coyote howls, loon wail, beaver slap); crow flap; clay break; scarecrow\n954\tbonk; snowball splat; UI focus tick, confirm, back; score ticks; banner whoosh; stink; slow-mo whoosh.\n955\tA Sound Lab dev scene plays every song, sfx and voice for review.\n956\t\n957\t### 5.21 Attract mode and the HunterBot (`95-attract.js`)\n958\t\n959\t**Idle detection**: any key, mouse button, mouse movement over 3 px, wheel, pad button or stick past the dead zone, or\n960\ttouch resets it. After **10 s** idle on `title` or a top-level `menu` page, go to `attract`. Any input in `attract`\n961\treturns to `title` (the input is swallowed). On touch-only devices it runs the same.\n962\t\n963\t**Playlist** (loops; fixed seeds so it is the same every time; a DEMO banner and a blinking PRESS ANY BUTTON):\n964\t1. Hollow Creek site 1, bot playing, 35 s, then 8 s of its tally with Shot Charts.\n965\t2. Bugle Ridge site 2: scoped long shots with hold-breath, a call that freezes a bull, 25 s.\n966\t3. Saucer Season, 15 s.\n967\t4. Muskeg Lake trophy: Big Mo's charge, a heart shot, the Trophy Cam, 20 s.\n968\t5. The high-score tables (`cab.drawTable`), 8 s; the Lodge's trophy wall pan, 6 s; the title, 5 s.\n969\t\n970\t**HunterBot** (also the test driver and the balance tool; `bot.cheat` for the attract mode): picks the best visible\n971\tlegal target (bucks first, value over distance, the ones about to escape first; critters when no buck is up; never\n972\tdoes or protected critters, and never fires if the ray's first hit would be one), moves its reticle with a critically\n973\tdamped spring toward the target's vital zone with lead for motion (reaction delay and aim noise from the `bot` stream by\n974\tskill: novice, average, expert), scopes past 90 m, holds breath when scoped, calls when its target runs fast, fires\n975\twhen its error is under 2 px, pumps after every shot. Cheats in attract: infinite rounds, auto-pump, perfect aim,\n976\tsees through cover but only fires on clear rays.\n977\t\n978\t### 5.22 Dev mode (`96-dev.js`)\n979\t\n980\tReached from the pause menu's **Dev mode** item (any pausable scene), and by the deep link `#dev`. Choosing it resumes\n981\tthe game underneath and opens a Shell screen `dev` (HTML, engine-styled, works with pad, keys and mouse; sliders turn\n982\twith left/right; Appendix C adds `rows` to custom Shell screens and `hidden` to settings so these stay off the normal\n983\tSettings screen). The game keeps running behind it (game actions are held back while the screen is open), so changes\n984\tshow live; **Freeze** stops the sim.\n985\t\n986\t- **Live sliders** (each a `game.settings` key in a hidden `Dev` group, saved, read through `TUNING`): every row of\n987\t  Appendix A, with **Reset to defaults** (`game.settings.reset('Dev')`) and a reset per row (confirm on the row).\n988\t- **Tools** (buttons): Freeze / Unfreeze, Slow motion (0.25x), Skip segment, Bag all bucks, Spawn buck / doe /\n989\t  trophy / critter at the reticle (the terrain point under it), Kill all, Refill and infinite ammo, God mode (no doe\n990\t  penalty, no stink), Jump to hunt / site / trophy / bonus (pickers), Bot plays (novice / average / expert), Free\n991\t  camera, Animal Lab, Sound Lab, Unlock all trophies, Reset save data (asks first), Copy snapshot (logs JSON).\n992\t- **Overlays** (toggles): hit volumes and the last ray, occluder volumes, actor state labels and fear bars, paths with\n993\t  bearing/distance marks, the play fan, occlusion lines, the engine's frame-rate readout (`settings.showFps`).\n994\t- **Free camera**: WASD or the left stick moves, the mouse (held right button) or the right stick looks, Q/E or L1/R1\n995\t  for height; a readout of position (m) and bearing/distance from the current vantage, to author paths; cancel exits.\n996\t- **Animal Lab** (`#animallab`): every species, sex, critter and person, every gait and pose, turntable and distance\n997\t  sliders, x-ray and mount previews. **Sound Lab** (`#soundlab`): plays every song, layer, sting, sfx and voice.\n998\t\n999\t**Tests** (flow/dev): the pause menu lists Dev mode; opening it shows screen `dev`; setting `dev.animalSpeed` to 2\n1000\tdoubles a walking deer's speed within one step; Reset to defaults restores every Dev key; God mode prevents benching;\n1001\tJump to site loads it; Free camera moves the lens.\n1002\t\n1003\t### 5.23 Settings and accessibility\n1004\tOur settings (in `menu.settings`, group Game): Difficulty (Easy/Normal/Pro), Aim assist (Off/Light/Strong), Reticle\n1005\tspeed (slider), Auto-pump (toggle), Scope (Hold/Toggle), Doe rule (Classic/Casual), Trophy Cam (On/Trophies only/Off),\n1006\tAntler glint (toggle), Large captions (toggle), Rival tag (toggle). The engine's standard ones stay: volume, music,\n1007\teffects, reduce motion (no shake, no camera flights, no slow-mo), screen shake, flashes, screen filter, button symbols,\n1008\tvibration, dead zone, rebinding. Information is never colour alone (reticle shapes, icons with text).\n1009\t\n1010\t### 5.24 Input map and game options (`01-game.js`)\n1011\t\n1012\t```js\n1013\tconst HUNT = {                       // our preset (game input option). Check game.input.map after creation: if the engine does\n1014\t                                     // not merge its own start/pause/confirm/cancel into a custom preset, add them here\n1015\t                                     // (start: Enter, Pad9; pause: Escape, KeyP, Pad9; confirm: Enter, Space, Pad0; cancel: Escape, Backspace, Pad1)\n1016\t  up: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'Pad12'], down: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'Pad13'], left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Pad14'], right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Pad15'],\n1017\t  fire:   ['Mouse0', 'Pad7', 'KeyJ'],          // left click, R2\n1018\t  pump:   ['KeyR', 'Space', 'Pad2', 'KeyK'],   // R, Space, Square\n1019\t  scope:  ['Mouse2', 'Pad6', 'KeyL'],          // right click, L2\n1020\t  breath: ['ShiftLeft', 'Pad5'],               // Shift, R1\n1021\t  call:   ['KeyQ', 'Pad3'],                    // Q, Triangle\n1022\t  board:  ['Tab', 'Pad8'],                     // hold: standings (unbound in hub rounds)\n1023\t};\n1024\tconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: [480, 270], expand: true, view: 'side', input: HUNT, id: 'bigbuckhuntoff',\n1025\t  menu: { items: [['Restart site', ...], ['Restart hunt', ...], ['Dev mode', () => dev.open()]], settings: [/* 5.23 */],\n1026\t          controls: { fire: 'Shoot', pump: 'Pump / reload', scope: 'Scope', breath: 'Hold breath', call: 'Call', board: 'Standings' },\n1027\t          quit: 'title' } });\n1028\t```\n1029\tEvery Vista scene sets `camera: { zoom: false }` (the wheel and -/= belong to the game), `touch: []`, and hides the OS\n1030\tcursor (the canvas has `cursor: none`; our reticle or a pixel arrow is drawn instead). The wheel (down) also pumps:\n1031\ta `wheel` listener calls `input.press('Act:pump')` and `input.release('Act:pump')` on the next step (or use the input\n1032\tchange in Appendix C). Menus: d-pad,\n1033\tleft stick, arrows/WASD move; Cross/Enter/Space confirm; Circle/Esc/Backspace back; L1/R1 or Q/E switch tabs; mouse\n1034\thover focuses and click picks.\n1035\t\n1036\t### 5.25 Touch-only devices\n1037\t`touchOnly = matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches`, re-checked when a\n1038\tkey, mouse or pad is used (then it is cleared for the visit). While true: no touch buttons anywhere (`touch: []`,\n1039\t`input.touchEnabled = false`), the title shows **Controller or keyboard required** in a big panel, the engine's corner\n1040\tmenu (settings) button stays usable, a tap does not start a game, and the attract mode runs after 10 s (a tap exits\n1041\tit to the title as any input does). **Tests** (flow/touch): with `matchMedia` stubbed to touch-only, the title shows the\n1042\tmessage, START does nothing from a tap, the attract mode starts after 10 s; a keydown clears it.\n1043\t\n1044\t### 5.26 AI Hub (`97-hub.js`): ghost mode\n1045\t\n1046\tWhy ghost: every player runs the same seeded hunt on their own device (fair, robust under latency and loss) and sees\n1047\tthe others' reticles and shots as ghosts, like players at one cabinet; scores race on the hub's board.\n1048\t\n1049\t**Flow** when `AIHub.active` (checked at startup; the session client is the page's first script):\n1050\t1. Boot step \"Calling the hub\": `info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If it is\n1051\t   `null`, start normally (title).\n1052\t2. Build the round's hunt: `hunt = ['hollow', 'bugle', 'muskeg'][((info.round || 1) - 1) % 3]` (rounds count from\n1053\t   1; keep the index non-negative); the run seed from `AIHub.rng('hunt')`. `AIHub.active` is known synchronously at\n1054\t   load, so `01-game.js` creates the engine with `autoPause: false`, `corner: false` and `menu.quit: false` when it is\n1055\t   true; the `hub` scene is not pausable; there is no title, attract or menu. (If `connect()` then answers `null`, the\n1056\t   game simply runs its normal title with those options; nothing else changes.)\n1057\t3. Scene `hub`, **our own card**: a lodge chalkboard over the hunt's vista: BIG BUCK HUNT-OFF, the hunt's name, the\n1058\t   players in their seat colours with ready ticks (from the `card` event's `ready`), how to win (\"Most points in 3\n1059\t   minutes. Bucks only, never does!\"), this player's controls as glyphs, the time left (`left`). Enter, Cross or a\n1060\t   click on READY -> `AIHub.answer('ready')`; Triangle, M or a click on MORE TIME -> `AIHub.answer('more')`. No\n1061\t   randomness except `AIHub.rng('card')`. `AIHub.ready()` is called as soon as the hunt is built (no key press).\n1062\t4. On `start`: a 3-2-1 from `AIHub.time()` (negative during the countdown); play begins at time 0.\n1063\t5. **The Hub Hunt-Off timeline** (3:00; every segment time-boxed and keyed to `AIHub.time()`, so all copies stay in\n1064\t   the same segment): 0:00-0:06 establishing pan and BUCKS ONLY!; 0:06-1:00 site A; 1:00-1:05 walk-in; 1:05-1:55 site\n1065\t   B; 1:55-2:00 walk-in; 2:00-2:30 the hunt's bonus game; 2:30-2:55 the trophy (time-boxed); 2:55-3:00 final tally,\n1066\t   then `AIHub.result({ score, stats: { 'Bucks bagged': n, Accuracy: '72%', 'Longest shot': '143 m' } })`.\n1067\t   Sites A/B: Hollow 1+2, Bugle 1+3, Muskeg 1+3. A doe benches the player until the next segment.\n1068\t6. **Clock**: each frame, if the local segment clock drifts more than 0.25 s from `AIHub.time()`, advance extra fixed\n1069\t   steps (catching up, no draw) or hold; past 2 s behind (a hidden tab), jump to the segment the hub clock is in.\n1070\t7. **Reporting**: `AIHub.progress({ score, label: 'Site 2 · 3 bucks' })` once a second; `result` once at the end or at\n1071\t   `time-up` (at once, with the current score, if not sent).\n1072\t8. **Ghosts**: 10 times a second, `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', s: segment, a: [yawMilli, pitchMilli], sc: scoped, p: score },\n1073\t   { reliable: false })` (aim as angles from the scripted camera); on each shot, a reliable `{ t: 'shot', s, a, res:\n1074\t   'buck' | 'doe' | 'critter' | 'miss', pts, zone }`. Received ghosts draw as their seat-colour reticle shape at 60%\n1075\t   opacity with the name under it (drawn in the pixel font; names are never put in HTML), their shots as small puffs\n1076\t   and \"+pts\" in their colour; a standings strip shows everyone's latest score. Ghosts never touch the local world.\n1077\t   `leave` removes a ghost.\n1078\t9. On `end`: stop input, stop music and sounds, show ROUND OVER with `standings` (names and colours) until the hub\n1079\t   removes the page. No alerts, dialogs, popups, new windows, sockets or fetches, ever.\n1080\t10. Create + Options belongs to the hub: nothing is bound to Create (Pad8) in sessions, and Options is ignored while\n1081\t    Create is held.\n1082\t\n1083\t**Tests**: flow/hub (headless, `tests/lib/hubstub.mjs`: a fake `AIHub` with a controllable clock and event emitter):\n1084\tconnect -> card drawn -> `ready()` called once without input -> `start` -> segments change on the hub clock ->\n1085\tprogress at least once a second -> exactly one result (also on early `time-up`) -> `end` stops input; ghost sends at\n1086\tmost 10/s unreliable plus shot events; spawns are identical in two copies that shoot differently (spawn logs equal);\n1087\t`Math.random` consumption by cosmetics doesn't change spawns. browser/hub: the real harness (section 9.4).\n1088\t\n1089\t### 5.27 About & Credits and the reports (`94-about.js`)\n1090\tPages (one idea per page, big text, L1/R1 or left/right to turn, back to leave): SOURCE INFORMATION (every field of\n1091\tTASK.md's list: date, source, plan, genre and perspective, tech, art direction, animation, audio, online, testing,\n1092\tresearch, environment, model, usage), TESTING FEEDBACK, ENGINE FEEDBACK, PROMPT FEEDBACK (the answers to TASK.md's\n1093\tquestions, written by the builders at the end), CREDITS (my-3D2dge v0.85.2 by Michael Crosato, MIT; Kenney asset\n1094\tentries used, CC0; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; \"all music, sounds and voices synthesized in code\"; the cast).\n1095\tThe same text goes in the final chat reply and in `exit-interview.json` (Appendix E).\n1096\t\n1097\t---\n1098\t\n1099\t## 6. Content\n1100\t\n1101\t### 6.1 Hunts and maps\n1102\t\n1103\t| Hunt | Species | Time and weather | Host / rival | Map (1024 m core) |\n1104\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1105\t| **Hollow Creek** | whitetail deer | autumn morning, valley mist, falling leaves | Uncle Dub; Granny Mae hosts the bonus | rolling hardwood hills; a creek meanders north to south; Granny Mae's farm (red barn, cornfield, pasture, fences) in the south-east; a hardwood ridge in the west; Fog Glade, a clearing in the north-west |\n1106\t| **Bugle Ridge** | elk | alpine dusk, sun behind the peaks | Loretta at the trap house | a high meadow ringed by aspens; a valley with a talus slope opposite; a timberline saddle to the west; a lake below; peaks in the Backdrop |\n1107\t| **Muskeg Lake** | moose | first snow, overcast, fog banks | Big Earl by the lake fire | a lake with reed shallows and a beaver lodge; spruce bog to the north; a burned clearing with charred snags to the east; a snowy shore |\n1108\t\n1109\tVantages per hunt (positions in metres in the core; authored with the dev free camera): three site vantages, the\n1110\ttrophy vantage and the bonus vantage, linked by trail paths for the walk-ins.\n1111\t\n1112\t### 6.2 Sites\n1113\t\n1114\t| Site | Vantage | FOV | Distances | Bucks | Time | Spawns (outline) | Critters |\n1115\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1116\t| Hollow 1 **Creek Crossing** | tree stand 4.5 m up over a ford | 34° | 18-50 m | 3 | 60 s | a doe and fawn cross first; a 6-pointer grazes on the bank, drinks; two bucks bound across the ford with a doe between them | squirrel on an oak (50), rabbit (75) |\n1117\t| Hollow 2 **Cornfield Edge** | ground blind at the field corner | 28° | 30-90 m | 4 | 70 s | pairs burst out of the corn rows (emerge), run the fence line; one jumps the fence; a 10-pointer last | turkeys x3 (150), skunk (-100), Bessie the cow (-500) |\n1118\t| Hollow 3 **Hardwood Ridge** | rock outcrop on the ridge | 32° | 25-70 m | 4 | 75 s | deer weave between trunks (wait for gaps); a buck bedded behind a log bolts at the first shot; a decoy doe | raccoon in a log (100), squirrels (50) |\n1119\t| Bugle 1 **Aspen Park** | knoll above the meadow | 28° | 40-80 m | 3 | 75 s | a herd of 8 cows with 2 bulls grazes; a satellite bull bugles in the aspens and steps out when called | marmot (75), grouse flush (150), eagle (-400) |\n1120\t| Bugle 2 **Talus Slope** | across the valley | 22° | 100-180 m | 3 | 75 s | elk traverse the far slope (scope and hold breath); rockfall startles them | coyote on the ridge (250) |\n1121\t| Bugle 3 **Timberline Saddle** | facing the sunset | 26° | 50-90 m | 4 | 70 s | groups cross the saddle as backlit silhouettes; a bull charges downhill toward you, then veers | grouse (150), marmot (75) |\n1122\t| Muskeg 1 **Reed Shallows** | a canoe offshore (bobbing) | 30° | 35-80 m | 2 (+3 cows, a calf) | 70 s | moose wade through reeds (legs below the water); a cow and calf cross close | ducks (150), beaver (100), loons (-400) |\n1123\t| Muskeg 2 **Spruce Bog** | a bog edge in fog | 36° | 20-50 m | 3 | 70 s | fog banks drift; moose loom out close; one stands and stares instead of running | snowshoe hare (125), raven (100) |\n1124\t| Muskeg 3 **Burn Clearing** | a snowy rise over the burn | 26° | 50-110 m | 3 | 75 s | moose trot across; two bulls lock antlers (fight) then split; a wolf pack chases a cow through (don't hit her) | wolves x3 (300), raven (100) |\n1125\t\n1126\tFOV is the vertical field of view in degrees, telephoto-ish so animals read at 480 x 270: at 28° a whitetail (head\n1127\tup, about 23 units tall before the `animalScale` boost) is about 26 px tall at 30 m, 16 px at 50 m and 10 px at 80 m,\n1128\twhere the scope (x3.5) makes it 34 px. Keep most shots inside 90 m; longer ones are scope shots by design.\n1129\t\n1130\t### 6.3 Trophies\n1131\t\n1132\t| Trophy | Where | Rules |\n1133\t|---|---|---|\n1134\t| **Old Iron Rack** (14-point whitetail) | Fog Glade at dawn, 60-100 m, 45 s | appears in 3 windows of 3.5 s between fog banks; a doe walks in front of him in window 3; he ignores calls until window 3 (then freezes 1.0 s) |\n1135\t| **The Duke of Bugle Ridge** (7 x 7 bull elk) | dark timber edge, 70-120 m, 50 s | he bugles from the trees (panned left or right so you can hear where); each of your calls draws him to the next opening for 4 s (4 openings); a cow leads him through the second; calling a fifth time sends him off |\n1136\t| **Big Mo** (72-inch bull moose) | the lake shore, 110 m in to 20 m, 45 s | bursts from the reeds and charges the stand over about 8 s; a lethal hit drops him; a gut or ham hit slows him; at 15 m he flattens the stand (screen tilt and crash: BIG MO SAYS NO!) and the trophy is lost; if missed he retreats and charges again, three times |\n1137\t\n1138\t### 6.4 Bonus games (30 s each)\n1139\t\n1140\t| Bonus | Host | Targets and rules |\n1141\t|---|---|---|\n1142\t| **Crow Patrol** (Hollow) | Granny Mae on her porch | crows flap up from Granny's corn in bursts, swoop and land on Hank the scarecrow: crows 100, the golden crow 500; hitting Hank -250 (\"Hank's got feelin's!\"); 10 rounds, rack 0.15 s |\n1143\t| **Saucer Season** (Bugle) | Loretta at the trap house | clay saucers from the trap: singles, doubles, crossing pairs, a high tower; 75 each, golden clay 500; 12 rounds |\n1144\t| **Snowball Standoff** (Muskeg) | Big Earl | snowmen pop up behind drifts and lob snowballs at you: shoot snowballs in the air (75) and knock hats off (150); a snowball that lands splats over part of the screen for 2 s; at 20 s the Snowmoose rises (a giant snow moose: its top hat 1000); 12 rounds |\n1145\t\n1146\tEach has a PERFECT bonus (every target hit, no misses: the bonus total doubles) and its own high-score table.\n1147\t\n1148\t### 6.5 Practice Range (Uncle Dub's)\n1149\tA flat field with berms and paper targets (custom props whose hit zones are flat rings), 7 stations, each a short line\n1150\tfrom Dub, an objective, and a check:\n1151\t1. **Aim and fire**: three paper bucks at 20 m.\n1152\t2. **Pump**: fire, pump, fire; then empty the tube and reload.\n1153\t3. **Shot placement**: a paper buck with the vital ring: put one in the heart (the zone callout shows).\n1154\t4. **Bucks only**: a moving target track alternating paper bucks and does: shoot only bucks (a doe hit is explained,\n1155\t   not punished).\n1156\t5. **Scope and breath**: a 150 m target: hold the scope, hold breath, fire (each named by its glyph).\n1157\t6. **The call**: a mechanical deer runs a rail; call to stop it, then shoot.\n1158\t7. **Critters**: tin squirrels pop up; a tin skunk with a DON'T sign.\n1159\tThen \"You'll do. Go win that Hunt-Off.\" and the Range badge in the Lodge. Prompts always use the last device's glyphs.\n1160\t\n1161\t### 6.6 Species (gameplay numbers)\n1162\t\n1163\t| Species | Target / protected | Shoulder, length | Walk / trot / run (m/s) | Antlers | hp | Points |\n1164\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1165\t| whitetail | buck / doe, fawn | 1.0 m, 1.8 m | 1.3 / 3.4 / 8.5 | 4-12 points; trophy 14 | 1 | 100 + 15/point |\n1166\t| elk | bull / cow, calf | 1.5 m, 2.4 m | 1.4 / 4.0 / 9.0 | 5x5 to 6x6; trophy 7x7 | 1.5 | 150 + 20/point |\n1167\t| moose | bull / cow, calf | 1.9 m, 2.9 m | 1.5 / 4.5 / 8.0 (charge 9.5) | 40-55 in spread; trophy 72 in | 2 | 200 + 6/inch |\n1168\t\n1169\t### 6.7 Critters (12 designs)\n1170\t\n1171\t| Critter | Rig | Behaviour | Points | Hunts |\n1172\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1173\t| squirrel | Blob (cat ears, bushy tail, feet) | climbs a trunk, runs a log, chatters | 50 | Hollow |\n1174\t| rabbit / snowshoe hare | Blob (rabbit ears, feet) | hops in arcs, freezes, bolts (hare is white) | 75 / 125 | Hollow / Muskeg |\n1175\t| wild turkey | Blob + fan and wattle | struts, gobbles, runs, flushes | 150 | Hollow |\n1176\t| raccoon | Blob + mask, ringed tail | peeks from a hollow log, ducks back | 100 | Hollow |\n1177\t| skunk (protected) | Blob + stripe | waddles; if shot: stink cloud | -100 | Hollow |\n1178\t| Bessie the cow (protected) | Quadruped cow | grazes in the pasture, moos | -500 | Hollow |\n1179\t| crow / raven | Blob bird | flies over in loose flocks, caws | 100 | Hollow bonus / Muskeg |\n1180\t| grouse | Blob bird | flushes from cover with a whirr, flies low | 150 | Bugle |\n1181\t| marmot | Blob | pops up on rocks, whistles, ducks | 75 | Bugle |\n1182\t| coyote / wolf | Quadruped canid | trots the ridge, howls; wolves chase in a pack | 250 / 300 | Bugle / Muskeg |\n1183\t| eagle (protected) | Blob bird, big | soars in circles high up | -400 | Bugle |\n1184\t| duck / loon (protected) / beaver | Blob bird; Blob swimmer | ducks flush and fly; loons float and wail; the beaver swims with a wake and slaps | 150 / -400 / 100 | Muskeg |\n1185\t\n1186\t### 6.8 Cast and story beats\n1187\t\n1188\t**Cast**: the Emcee (announcer of the Hunt-Off), Uncle Dub (your guide), Granny Mae (farm owner, Crow Patrol host),\n1189\tCousin Dwayne (rival, boastful), Loretta Pruitt (rival, sharp and kind), Big Earl (rival, here for the chili).\n1190\t\n1191\t| Beat | When | Lines (write more in the same voice; keep each under about 60 characters) |\n1192\t|---|---|---|\n1193\t| welcome | first Hunt-Off start | EMCEE: \"Welcome to the 41st Annual Big Buck Hunt-Off!\" / EMCEE: \"Three hunts. One trophy wall. Zero does!\" / DUB: \"Name's Dub. Forty years guidin'. Lost twice. On purpose.\" |\n1194\t| rivals | after welcome | DWAYNE: \"Hope you packed a lunch, cuz. You'll be here a while.\" / LORETTA: \"Ignore him. He shot a mailbox in '09.\" / EARL: \"I'm mostly here for the chili.\" |\n1195\t| hollow intro | Hollow Creek start | DUB: \"Whitetails thick as ticks out here.\" / DUB: \"Bucks got antlers. Does don't. Can't tell? Don't pull.\" / DUB: \"Pump after every shot. This rifle's older'n me.\" |\n1196\t| iron rack legend | before the trophy | DUB: \"Old Iron Rack. Fourteen points.\" / DUB: \"Walks in the fog so nobody can count 'em.\" / DUB: \"Been dodgin' hunters since your daddy wore diapers.\" |\n1197\t| crow patrol | before the bonus | GRANNY: \"Crows ate my sweet corn. Every last ear!\" / GRANNY: \"Shoot the crows, sugar. Not Hank.\" |\n1198\t| hollow outro | after results | DWAYNE (behind): \"Scope's crooked. That's all that is.\" or DWAYNE (ahead): \"Told ya. Bring a lunch.\" |\n1199\t| bugle intro | Bugle Ridge start | DUB: \"Elk hear a bugle, they come lookin' for a fight.\" / DUB: \"Give 'em a call and they'll stop to see who's talkin'.\" |\n1200\t| duke legend | before the trophy | DUB: \"The Duke don't come out for just anybody.\" / DUB: \"Answer him back. Make him curious.\" |\n1201\t| saucer season | before the bonus | LORETTA: \"Pull!... That's what you say. Then you shoot it.\" |\n1202\t| muskeg intro | Muskeg Lake start | DUB: \"Moose ain't skittish. Moose is a truck with opinions.\" / EARL: \"Chili's on the fire if you live.\" |\n1203\t| big mo legend | before the trophy | DUB: \"Big Mo don't run from you.\" / DUB: \"He runs AT you. Hold steady.\" |\n1204\t| snowball standoff | before the bonus | EARL: \"The snowmen are back. They want revenge.\" |\n1205\t| ceremony | after Muskeg results | EMCEE: placement line (\"Our new Hunt-Off champion!\" / \"There's always next year!\"), DUB: \"Hang it on the wall, kid.\" Then the Lodge with the new mounts, then the credits page |\n1206\t\n1207\t### 6.9 Barks (emcee unless noted)\n1208\t\n1209\t| Category | Lines |\n1210\t|---|---|\n1211\t| start | BUCKS ONLY! / HERE THEY COME! / EYES SHARP, HUNTERS! / THREE BUCKS ON THE MOVE! (count from the site) |\n1212\t| kill | NICE SHOT! / BAGGED 'EM! / WHAT A SHOT! / DOWN HE GOES! |\n1213\t| zones | HEART SHOT! / HEADSHOT! / LUNG SHOT! / NECK SHOT! / SHOULDER! / GUT SHOT... FINISH HIM! |\n1214\t| long / running / quick | LONG SHOT! CALL THE PAPER! / RUNNING SHOT! / QUICK DRAW! |\n1215\t| multi | DOUBLE! / TRIPLE! THE CROWD GOES MILD! |\n1216\t| miss | MISSED HIM CLEAN! / THAT'S A LOT OF DIRT YOU KILLED! / BARK'S DEAD, BUCK AIN'T! |\n1217\t| pump / reload | PUMP IT! / RELOAD, HOSS! |\n1218\t| doe | DOE! YOU'RE OUT! / THAT'S A DOE! HOLSTER UP! / AW, NOT MAMA! / A FAWN?! GO SIT IN THE TRUCK! |\n1219\t| protected | OH, THE STINK! / THAT'S BESSIE!! / THAT'S THE NATIONAL BIRD, BUDDY! / NOT THE LOON! |\n1220\t| escape / lost | HE'S GETTIN' AWAY! / GONE LIKE A RUMOR! / WOUNDED AND LOST... |\n1221\t| trophy | TROPHY SPOTTED! / THAT'S OLD IRON RACK! / THE DUKE! / HERE COMES BIG MO! / TROPHY BAGGED! / THE ONE THAT GOT AWAY... |\n1222\t| end | SITE CLEAR! / TIME! / CLEAN SWEEP! |\n1223\t| critters | CRITTER BONUS! / SQUIRREL! / TURKEY DINNER! |\n1224\t| Dub (tips, quieter) | \"Wait for him to clear that tree.\" / \"Hold your breath. Steady as a church pew.\" / \"Give him a grunt.\" |\n1225\t\n1226\t### 6.10 Items and unlockables\n1227\tThere are no pickups or power-ups in play; the player's kit and the goals are:\n1228\t- **The kit**: the pump rifle (5-round tube), the scope, and a call per hunt (a grunt tube at Hollow Creek, a bugle at\n1229\t  Bugle Ridge, a moose call at Muskeg Lake), introduced by Dub in each hunt's briefing with its glyph.\n1230\t- **Special targets** that play the power-up role: the golden crow, the golden clay, the Snowmoose's hat; quick-draw,\n1231\t  long-shot and multi-kill bonuses.\n1232\t- **Unlockables kept in the Lodge**: the three trophy mounts, each hunt's best-buck plaque, stars per site (27 in all),\n1233\t  the Range badge, the Hunt-Off champion plaque (first place in the campaign), high-score entries with initials.\n1234\t- Everything is playable from the start (no locked hunts): the demo must show all of it.\n1235\t\n1236\t---\n1237\t\n1238\t## 7. Build order and milestones\n1239\t\n1240\tBuild the spine first, one hunt to a full vertical slice, then widen. Each milestone ends with its tests passing\n1241\t(`node tests/run.mjs`) and, where it says so, screenshots looked at.\n1242\t\n1243\t| # | Milestone | Delivers | Done when |\n1244\t|---|---|---|---|\n1245\t| M0 | Setup | dev folder, engine and hub copies, manifest, build script, dev page, test runner and headless loader, `game.debug` stub with snapshot | `node tests/run.mjs` runs (one smoke test); the bundle opens from `file://` with no errors |\n1246\t| M1 | Gallery on a flat floor | E.Lens, Vista with flat terrain, Backdrop sky, billboards with impostors (library trees and rocks), static deer silhouettes, P1 reticle (mouse and pad), fire with analytic sphere hits, a minimal HUD | shooting a silhouette works by mouse and pad; lens tests pass; screenshot looks like a pixel landscape |\n1247\t| M2 | The deer | E.Quadruped whitetail (skeleton, 4 gaits, poses, antlers, outline, LOD, zones, x-ray, mount), Animal Lab | quadruped tests pass; filmstrips of every gait and the death look right |\n1248\t| M3 | The land | E.Heightfield (base, features, water, ground types, light bake, scatter, occluders), terrain raster with occlusion, water, fog and mist, Hollow Creek map, custom props (corn, reeds, tall grass, birch, barn, stand, blind) | terrain and occlusion tests pass; Hollow's three vantages screenshot well; animals hide behind crests |\n1249\t| M4 | Shooting for real | rifle (pump, tube, reload), scope lens with sway and breath, call, aim assist, full shot resolution with zones, occluders, terrain and water, impacts and particles, scoring v1, banners and pops | weapon, aim, shot and score tests pass; pick-agreement check at 95% |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3fa61e8-1431-4900-ae89-edc59162574b","uuid":"5469f2ad-9063-4412-8db7-8505e613542a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:06:09.506Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050554__x4cdb93/work/PLAN.md","content":"- Shared camera (director keyframes only), shared animals, first hit takes it; each player has their own rifle, calls,\n  score, stats; benching is per player (benched players watch); the site's end rules (5.7) apply to everyone.\n- The tally shows a column per player; hunt results show a podium; the winner may enter initials.\n- A pad unplugged pauses with the engine's message (per player).\n\n**Tests** (flow/party): two and four scripted players join; each has its own tube and score; a doe benches only its\nshooter; a shared kill splits points; the podium orders players by score.\n\n### 5.12 HUD, prompts and glyphs (`51-hud.js`, `52-glyphs.js`)\n\n10-foot rules: the HUD is sparse and large. At 480 x 270: key numbers at font scale 2 (14 px), banners at scale 3-4,\ncaptions at scale 1 with a shadow in a dark band; 12 px safe margins; clear of `game.cornerArea()` and, on a phone,\n`input.touchArea()`.\n\n- **Top centre**: site name and clock (0:42); under it a row of buck icons (antler silhouettes: hollow = to come,\n  filled in the bagger's colour = bagged, crossed = escaped or lost).\n- **Player panels** (P1 bottom left, P2 bottom right, P3 top left, P4 top right): score, five shell icons with a\n  chamber light, call charges (horn icons), breath arc while scoped, BENCHED tag.\n- **Centre banners**: BUCKS ONLY!, HEART SHOT!, DOE! YOU'RE OUT!, TROPHY!, TIME!, with an extruded `E.font.title`\n  style, 0.9 s, a whoosh.\n- **Score pops** in the world over the animal: \"+425 HEART SHOT 86 m\" in the shooter's colour.\n- **Captions** (barks and dialog) lower centre with the speaker's name and colour.\n- **Prompts** lower centre, contextual (PUMP!, HOLD [L2] TO SCOPE, CALL [△]), shown only when relevant and for a\n  limited number of times per hunt.\n- **Rival tag** (campaign): top left under P3's place: \"DWAYNE 4,600\".\n- **Hold to see standings** (Tab or Create; unbound in hub rounds): a centre table of players' scores.\n\n**Glyphs**: `Prompts.label(action, player)` decides the family by the player's last device: `gamepad` -> the pad's\nglyph (`input.label(action, 'gamepad')` gives '✕', '○', '□', '△', 'R2', 'L2', 'R1', 'L1' with PlayStation symbols, or\n'A', 'B', 'X', 'Y', 'RT', 'LT', 'RB', 'LB' with Xbox); `keyboard` or `mouse` -> one KB+M family: actions bound to a\nmouse button show the mouse icon once the mouse has been used this session, others show the key (R, Q, Shift, Space,\nEsc, Tab, Enter). `52-glyphs.js` draws each as a pixel icon: PS shapes in their colours (blue cross, red circle, pink\nsquare, green triangle) on dark discs, trigger and bumper tabs, stick icons, Options and Create pills; Xbox letters on\ncoloured discs; keycaps (wide for Space, Shift, Enter); a mouse with the left, right or wheel highlighted. The default\nbutton symbols are **PlayStation**; Settings > Controller > Button symbols offers Xbox (engine setting, default changed:\nAppendix C).\n\n**Tests** (unit/prompts): with a pad last used, labels are PlayStation glyphs by default and Xbox letters after\n`settings.set('glyphs', 'xbox')`; with the mouse used, fire shows the left-click icon and pump shows R; every action\nthe HUD prompts has an icon in all three families; every caption and banner fits the screen width at its scale\n(`E.font.width`).\n\n### 5.13 Feedback and juice\n- Shot: a 1-2 px screen shake (comfort setting respected), reticle bloom, gunshot with a valley echo (5.20), a pad\n  rumble (0.35, 0.08 s) for the shooter.\n- Kill: hit-stop 0.04 s (`game.freeze`), callout banner for lethal zones, score pop, the bagged tag; a stronger rumble.\n- Doe: a red-tinted flash (flashes setting respected), the sad-trombone sting, the emcee's groan, the BENCHED reticle.\n- Multi-kills, long shots (150 m and more: LONG SHOT!), running shots: their own barks.\n- **Trophy Cam** (trophy kills, and in single player the last buck of a site if it was a heart shot; setting On /\n  Trophies only / Off): the sim runs at `game.timeScale = 0.15` while the camera flight takes 1.4 s of unscaled time\n  (`game.real`): the lens flies from the vantage along the shot's ray to 3 m from the impact, the fov narrows, a\n  bullet streak leads; at impact the animal flashes to its x-ray look (skeleton, heart and lungs) for 0.35 s; normal\n  speed for its collapse; back to the vantage with a fade; time scale restored. Skippable (confirm). Never during\n  local multiplayer or hub rounds (they show the Shot Chart only). Under Reduce motion it is a still x-ray card.\n- Skunk: a green dithered cloud over 60% of the screen fading over 3 s, a \"pfft\" and a stink chord.\n\n### 5.14 Tally and the Shot Chart (`60-tally.js`)\nA full-screen card over the dimmed, frozen vista, one beat at a time (10-foot friendly), confirm to skip ahead:\n1. SITE CLEAR or TIME!, the site's name.\n2. For each bagged animal, a card: its x-ray side view (`rig.drawXray`: a dithered translucent body, skeleton lines,\n   heart red and lungs pink, entry marks where each round went, labelled HEART / LUNG / GUT...), its distance, antler\n   points or spread, and its points line counted up with ticks.\n3. Critters, penalties, accuracy, clean sweep, no-penalty bonus, site total; the stars (antler icons) pop in.\n4. Party: a column per player, then the site's leader. Campaign: the standings strip against the rivals.\nPrompt: [✕] CONTINUE (per device). Confirm is ignored for the first 0.6 s (Space pumps in play and confirms here, so\na late pump doesn't skip a card). Auto-advances after 12 s in the attract mode.\n\n### 5.15 Trophy encounters (`61-trophy.js`)\nA trophy site is a site with a legend, one named animal and rules of its own (6.3). Shared parts: a campfire legend\ndialog before it (Uncle Dub), tension music layers in when the trophy is on screen, the trophy shows a TROPHY tag the\nfirst time it's seen, its HUD icon is gold, it has 1.5x the species' hp and ignores the call except where its rules\nsay, and a miss makes it bolt (its window ends). Bagged: Trophy Cam, TROPHY BAGGED!, x3 points, its mount unlocks in\nthe Lodge. Escaped: THE ONE THAT GOT AWAY (no penalty). Saved in records either way (seen, bagged, best distance).\n\n### 5.16 Bonus games (`62-bonus.js`)\nA framework for 30-second shooting galleries on the same landscape at a bonus vantage: a target spawner on a\ntimeline, thrown or flying targets on ballistic arcs (`E.arc`-style maths in world space) or `E.Path`s, the same rifle\nrules with a bigger tube and faster rack, per-target points, protected targets with penalties, a PERFECT bonus (every\ntarget hit with no misses doubles the bonus total), and a bonus tally. The three games are in 6.4. Bonus Only mode plays\nany of them from the menu; they keep their own high-score tables.\n\n### 5.17 Modes and menus (`90-title.js`, `91-menu.js`, `92-hunt.js`, `94-about.js`, `53-ui.js`)\n\n**Title**: the logo (`E.font.title`, wood-and-brass gradient with a blaze-orange outline, \"THE 41ST ANNUAL\" above it)\nover a live vista (Hollow Creek at dawn, deer grazing, slow pan); PRESS [START] in the last device's glyph; the\nengine's corner menu button (settings) at top right. CONTINUE appears in the menu when an autosaved Hunt-Off exists.\n\n**Main menu** (big cards, one column, focus with d-pad, stick or arrows; hover with the mouse moves the focus; click or\nconfirm picks; cancel goes back; a prompt bar at the bottom shows confirm and back glyphs):\n\n| Entry | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| HUNT-OFF (or CONTINUE HUNT-OFF) | the campaign: Hollow Creek, Bugle Ridge, Muskeg Lake in order, rivals and standings, ceremony; autosave after each hunt (`game.saves` autosave slot) |\n| SINGLE HUNT | pick one of the three hunts (card with species, time of day, trophy silhouette, best score) |\n| PARTY HUNT | the join page (players press Options or Start on their pads; the mouse player is P1), then pick a hunt or QUICK DRAW (site 1 of each hunt plus Saucer Season, time-boxed; a short loading card raises each landscape between them) |\n| BONUS GAMES | pick Crow Patrol, Saucer Season or Snowball Standoff |\n| PRACTICE RANGE | Uncle Dub's range: the tutorial (6.5) |\n| THE LODGE | the trophy room (5.18) |\n| SETTINGS | the engine's settings screen (`game.menu('settings')`) |\n| ABOUT & CREDITS | 5.27 |\n\n**Difficulty** (picked on the hunt card, remembered): Easy (Strong assist, auto-pump, animals x0.85 speed, +1 call),\nNormal, Pro (no assist, animals x1.15 speed, does mixed in more often, scope sway x1.3).\n\n### 5.18 The Lodge, records and saves (`93-lodge.js`)\n- A cozy side-view room built with the engine's own 2D pipeline: a `side` view, a PlatformMap floor of `wood` tiles and\n  a log back wall (`back` tiles, `plank` material), engine props and shapes (fireplace from custom shape, table, chairs,\n  bench, bookcase, barrel, lamps; `light: true`), warm canvas lighting with a flickering fire, Uncle Dub in a rocking\n  chair (Humanoid, idle; waves when focused), a sleeping hound (Blob).\n- The trophy wall: plaques for Old Iron Rack, The Duke, Big Mo (dark silhouettes until bagged, then `rig.drawMount`),\n  each hunt's best buck, and the records chalkboard (E.Arcade tables per mode with initials, preloaded with DUB, MAE,\n  DWN, LOR, ERL). Focus moves along the wall (d-pad, stick, arrows, mouse hover); the camera pans to it; a big info\n  card shows its story, distance, date bagged.\n- Stats card: hunts played, shots, accuracy, bucks bagged, does shot, longest shot, favourite rifle sound (a joke line).\n- `Records` in `E.store`: best scores per mode and hunt, stars per site, trophies, stats, the Range badge. In AI Hub\n  sessions storage is a throwaway memory store (the client's), so nothing special is needed.\n\n### 5.19 Dialog, barks and voices (`71-barks.js`, `babble.js`)\n- **Dialog** scenes use `E.Dialog` with Humanoid portraits; `voice: null` and our Babble voice plays the line. Story\n  beats are data (`def('beat', ...)`): a list of `[speaker, line]` with optional pose and expression.\n- **Barks**: categories (6.9) with 3-6 lines each; picked without repeating the last two (fx stream); the emcee shouts\n  them as a caption plus a short Babble burst; at most one bark per 1.2 s, high-priority barks (doe, trophy, triple)\n  cut in.\n- **E.Babble** (Animalese/Simlish style): each line becomes syllables (letter pairs; vowels pick the pitch step),\n  12-16 syllables a second, each a 40-70 ms blip through a band-pass \"formant\" filter per vowel; per character: base\n  pitch, waveform, speed, pitch spread, warble. Exclamations rise at the end; questions rise; ALL-CAPS barks are louder\n  and faster. Voices: Emcee (140 Hz square, boomy, echo), Uncle Dub (105 Hz saw with noise grit, slow), Granny Mae (260\n  Hz sine with vibrato), Dwayne (185 Hz 12.5% pulse, nasal), Loretta (225 Hz triangle, bright), Earl (95 Hz square,\n  slow and warm). Uses `game.audio.ctx` and the exposed sfx bus (Appendix C); silent headless.\n\n### 5.20 Audio (`70-audio.js`)\n\n**Music** (engine song notation; bluegrass chiptune):\n\n| Song | Where | Sketch |\n|---|---|---|\n| `hoedown` | title, menus | 140 bpm, G major: pulse-25% banjo rolls in 16ths, square fiddle melody, triangle root-fifth bass, washboard noise and rimshots |\n| `lodgefire` | Lodge, About | 84 bpm, warm square \"harmonica\" with vibrato over triangle chords, soft brushes |\n| `stalk` | hunt sites (layers) | 96 bpm pads and pulse ostinato at low volume; layer `drums` comes in when bucks are on screen, layer `tension` (heartbeat kick, tremolo) when a trophy is on screen (`audio.layer`) |\n| `jamboree` | bonus games | 160 bpm hoedown, fast fiddle |\n| `results` | tallies, hunt results | 110 bpm strut |\n| `fanfare`, `siteclear`, `doe`, `escaped`, `newrecord` | stings (`audio.sting`) | trophy fanfare; clear jingle; sad trombone slide; two-note fall; initials theme |\n\n**Ambience** beds per hunt: wind (filtered noise, slow swells), birdsong chirps (random sine and pulse blips by time of\nday), creek or lake lapping, distant crows (Hollow), elk chirps and distant bugles (Bugle), loon calls and ice creaks\n(Muskeg).\n\n**SFX** (engine voices, lists with `delay` for layering): rifle shot (noise crack 0.05 s high-passed + 60 Hz sine\nthump 0.15 s + low noise tail 0.6 s + two echoes at 0.35 s and 0.8 s, quieter and darker, the echo delay longer across\nopen valleys); dry click; pump rack (two band-passed clicks 0.09 s apart with a slide); shell inserts; scope raise\n(cloth swish); breath in and out; calls (grunt: 90 Hz saw wobble; bugle: sine 500 -> 1800 Hz glide with vibrato and\na noisy scream; moose: 70 Hz saw \"waugh\"); impacts (fur thump, wood knock, rock ricochet whine 3000 -> 1200 Hz,\ndirt thud, splash); hooves by gait; animal voices (snort, cow-elk chirp, turkey gobble trill, duck quack, crow caw,\nsquirrel chatter, marmot whistle, wolf and coyote howls, loon wail, beaver slap); crow flap; clay break; scarecrow\nbonk; snowball splat; UI focus tick, confirm, back; score ticks; banner whoosh; stink; slow-mo whoosh.\nA Sound Lab dev scene plays every song, sfx and voice for review.\n\n### 5.21 Attract mode and the HunterBot (`95-attract.js`)\n\n**Idle detection**: any key, mouse button, mouse movement over 3 px, wheel, pad button or stick past the dead zone, or\ntouch resets it. After **10 s** idle on `title` or a top-level `menu` page, go to `attract`. Any input in `attract`\nreturns to `title` (the input is swallowed). On touch-only devices it runs the same.\n\n**Playlist** (loops; fixed seeds so it is the same every time; a DEMO banner and a blinking PRESS ANY BUTTON):\n1. Hollow Creek site 1, bot playing, 35 s, then 8 s of its tally with Shot Charts.\n2. Bugle Ridge site 2: scoped long shots with hold-breath, a call that freezes a bull, 25 s.\n3. Saucer Season, 15 s.\n4. Muskeg Lake trophy: Big Mo's charge, a heart shot, the Trophy Cam, 20 s.\n5. The high-score tables (`cab.drawTable`), 8 s; the Lodge's trophy wall pan, 6 s; the title, 5 s.\n\n**HunterBot** (also the test driver and the balance tool; `bot.cheat` for the attract mode): picks the best visible\nlegal target (bucks first, value over distance, the ones about to escape first; critters when no buck is up; never\ndoes or protected critters, and never fires if the ray's first hit would be one), moves its reticle with a critically\ndamped spring toward the target's vital zone with lead for motion (reaction delay and aim noise from the `bot` stream by\nskill: novice, average, expert), scopes past 90 m, holds breath when scoped, calls when its target runs fast, fires\nwhen its error is under 2 px, pumps after every shot. Cheats in attract: infinite rounds, auto-pump, perfect aim,\nsees through cover but only fires on clear rays.\n\n### 5.22 Dev mode (`96-dev.js`)\n\nReached from the pause menu's **Dev mode** item (any pausable scene), and by the deep link `#dev`. Choosing it resumes\nthe game underneath and opens a Shell screen `dev` (HTML, engine-styled, works with pad, keys and mouse; sliders turn\nwith left/right; Appendix C adds `rows` to custom Shell screens and `hidden` to settings so these stay off the normal\nSettings screen). The game keeps running behind it (game actions are held back while the screen is open), so changes\nshow live; **Freeze** stops the sim.\n\n- **Live sliders** (each a `game.settings` key in a hidden `Dev` group, saved, read through `TUNING`): every row of\n  Appendix A, with **Reset to defaults** (`game.settings.reset('Dev')`) and a reset per row (confirm on the row).\n- **Tools** (buttons): Freeze / Unfreeze, Slow motion (0.25x), Skip segment, Bag all bucks, Spawn buck / doe /\n  trophy / critter at the reticle (the terrain point under it), Kill all, Refill and infinite ammo, God mode (no doe\n  penalty, no stink), Jump to hunt / site / trophy / bonus (pickers), Bot plays (novice / average / expert), Free\n  camera, Animal Lab, Sound Lab, Unlock all trophies, Reset save data (asks first), Copy snapshot (logs JSON).\n- **Overlays** (toggles): hit volumes and the last ray, occluder volumes, actor state labels and fear bars, paths with\n  bearing/distance marks, the play fan, occlusion lines, the engine's frame-rate readout (`settings.showFps`).\n- **Free camera**: WASD or the left stick moves, the mouse (held right button) or the right stick looks, Q/E or L1/R1\n  for height; a readout of position (m) and bearing/distance from the current vantage, to author paths; cancel exits.\n- **Animal Lab** (`#animallab`): every species, sex, critter and person, every gait and pose, turntable and distance\n  sliders, x-ray and mount previews. **Sound Lab** (`#soundlab`): plays every song, layer, sting, sfx and voice.\n\n**Tests** (flow/dev): the pause menu lists Dev mode; opening it shows screen `dev`; setting `dev.animalSpeed` to 2\ndoubles a walking deer's speed within one step; Reset to defaults restores every Dev key; God mode prevents benching;\nJump to site loads it; Free camera moves the lens.\n\n### 5.23 Settings and accessibility\nOur settings (in `menu.settings`, group Game): Difficulty (Easy/Normal/Pro), Aim assist (Off/Light/Strong), Reticle\nspeed (slider), Auto-pump (toggle), Scope (Hold/Toggle), Doe rule (Classic/Casual), Trophy Cam (On/Trophies only/Off),\nAntler glint (toggle), Large captions (toggle), Rival tag (toggle). The engine's standard ones stay: volume, music,\neffects, reduce motion (no shake, no camera flights, no slow-mo), screen shake, flashes, screen filter, button symbols,\nvibration, dead zone, rebinding. Information is never colour alone (reticle shapes, icons with text).\n\n### 5.24 Input map and game options (`01-game.js`)\n\n```js\nconst HUNT = {                       // our preset (game input option). Check game.input.map after creation: if the engine does\n                                     // not merge its own start/pause/confirm/cancel into a custom preset, add them here\n                                     // (start: Enter, Pad9; pause: Escape, KeyP, Pad9; confirm: Enter, Space, Pad0; cancel: Escape, Backspace, Pad1)\n  up: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'Pad12'], down: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'Pad13'], left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Pad14'], right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Pad15'],\n  fire:   ['Mouse0', 'Pad7', 'KeyJ'],          // left click, R2\n  pump:   ['KeyR', 'Space', 'Pad2', 'KeyK'],   // R, Space, Square\n  scope:  ['Mouse2', 'Pad6', 'KeyL'],          // right click, L2\n  breath: ['ShiftLeft', 'Pad5'],               // Shift, R1\n  call:   ['KeyQ', 'Pad3'],                    // Q, Triangle\n  board:  ['Tab', 'Pad8'],                     // hold: standings (unbound in hub rounds)\n};\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: [480, 270], expand: true, view: 'side', input: HUNT, id: 'bigbuckhuntoff',\n  menu: { items: [['Restart site', ...], ['Restart hunt', ...], ['Dev mode', () => dev.open()]], settings: [/* 5.23 */],\n          controls: { fire: 'Shoot', pump: 'Pump / reload', scope: 'Scope', breath: 'Hold breath', call: 'Call', board: 'Standings' },\n          quit: 'title' } });\n```\nEvery Vista scene sets `camera: { zoom: false }` (the wheel and -/= belong to the game), `touch: []`, and hides the OS\ncursor (the canvas has `cursor: none`; our reticle or a pixel arrow is drawn instead). The wheel (down) also pumps:\na `wheel` listener calls `input.press('Act:pump')` and `input.release('Act:pump')` on the next step (or use the input\nchange in Appendix C). Menus: d-pad,\nleft stick, arrows/WASD move; Cross/Enter/Space confirm; Circle/Esc/Backspace back; L1/R1 or Q/E switch tabs; mouse\nhover focuses and click picks.\n\n### 5.25 Touch-only devices\n`touchOnly = matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches`, re-checked when a\nkey, mouse or pad is used (then it is cleared for the visit). While true: no touch buttons anywhere (`touch: []`,\n`input.touchEnabled = false`), the title shows **Controller or keyboard required** in a big panel, the engine's corner\nmenu (settings) button stays usable, a tap does not start a game, and the attract mode runs after 10 s (a tap exits\nit to the title as any input does). **Tests** (flow/touch): with `matchMedia` stubbed to touch-only, the title shows the\nmessage, START does nothing from a tap, the attract mode starts after 10 s; a keydown clears it.\n\n### 5.26 AI Hub (`97-hub.js`): ghost mode\n\nWhy ghost: every player runs the same seeded hunt on their own device (fair, robust under latency and loss) and sees\nthe others' reticles and shots as ghosts, like players at one cabinet; scores race on the hub's board.\n\n**Flow** when `AIHub.active` (checked at startup; the session client is the page's first script):\n1. Boot step \"Calling the hub\": `info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If it is\n   `null`, start normally (title).\n2. Build the round's hunt: `hunt = ['hollow', 'bugle', 'muskeg'][((info.round || 1) - 1) % 3]` (rounds count from\n   1; keep the index non-negative); the run seed from `AIHub.rng('hunt')`. `AIHub.active` is known synchronously at\n   load, so `01-game.js` creates the engine with `autoPause: false`, `corner: false` and `menu.quit: false` when it is\n   true; the `hub` scene is not pausable; there is no title, attract or menu. (If `connect()` then answers `null`, the\n   game simply runs its normal title with those options; nothing else changes.)\n3. Scene `hub`, **our own card**: a lodge chalkboard over the hunt's vista: BIG BUCK HUNT-OFF, the hunt's name, the\n   players in their seat colours with ready ticks (from the `card` event's `ready`), how to win (\"Most points in 3\n   minutes. Bucks only, never does!\"), this player's controls as glyphs, the time left (`left`). Enter, Cross or a\n   click on READY -> `AIHub.answer('ready')`; Triangle, M or a click on MORE TIME -> `AIHub.answer('more')`. No\n   randomness except `AIHub.rng('card')`. `AIHub.ready()` is called as soon as the hunt is built (no key press).\n4. On `start`: a 3-2-1 from `AIHub.time()` (negative during the countdown); play begins at time 0.\n5. **The Hub Hunt-Off timeline** (3:00; every segment time-boxed and keyed to `AIHub.time()`, so all copies stay in\n   the same segment): 0:00-0:06 establishing pan and BUCKS ONLY!; 0:06-1:00 site A; 1:00-1:05 walk-in; 1:05-1:55 site\n   B; 1:55-2:00 walk-in; 2:00-2:30 the hunt's bonus game; 2:30-2:55 the trophy (time-boxed); 2:55-3:00 final tally,\n   then `AIHub.result({ score, stats: { 'Bucks bagged': n, Accuracy: '72%', 'Longest shot': '143 m' } })`.\n   Sites A/B: Hollow 1+2, Bugle 1+3, Muskeg 1+3. A doe benches the player until the next segment.\n6. **Clock**: each frame, if the local segment clock drifts more than 0.25 s from `AIHub.time()`, advance extra fixed\n   steps (catching up, no draw) or hold; past 2 s behind (a hidden tab), jump to the segment the hub clock is in.\n7. **Reporting**: `AIHub.progress({ score, label: 'Site 2 · 3 bucks' })` once a second; `result` once at the end or at\n   `time-up` (at once, with the current score, if not sent).\n8. **Ghosts**: 10 times a second, `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', s: segment, a: [yawMilli, pitchMilli], sc: scoped, p: score },\n   { reliable: false })` (aim as angles from the scripted camera); on each shot, a reliable `{ t: 'shot', s, a, res:\n   'buck' | 'doe' | 'critter' | 'miss', pts, zone }`. Received ghosts draw as their seat-colour reticle shape at 60%\n   opacity with the name under it (drawn in the pixel font; names are never put in HTML), their shots as small puffs\n   and \"+pts\" in their colour; a standings strip shows everyone's latest score. Ghosts never touch the local world.\n   `leave` removes a ghost.\n9. On `end`: stop input, stop music and sounds, show ROUND OVER with `standings` (names and colours) until the hub\n   removes the page. No alerts, dialogs, popups, new windows, sockets or fetches, ever.\n10. Create + Options belongs to the hub: nothing is bound to Create (Pad8) in sessions, and Options is ignored while\n    Create is held.\n\n**Tests**: flow/hub (headless, `tests/lib/hubstub.mjs`: a fake `AIHub` with a controllable clock and event emitter):\nconnect -> card drawn -> `ready()` called once without input -> `start` -> segments change on the hub clock ->\nprogress at least once a second -> exactly one result (also on early `time-up`) -> `end` stops input; ghost sends at\nmost 10/s unreliable plus shot events; spawns are identical in two copies that shoot differently (spawn logs equal);\n`Math.random` consumption by cosmetics doesn't change spawns. browser/hub: the real harness (section 9.4).\n\n### 5.27 About & Credits and the reports (`94-about.js`)\nPages (one idea per page, big text, L1/R1 or left/right to turn, back to leave): SOURCE INFORMATION (every field of\nTASK.md's list: date, source, plan, genre and perspective, tech, art direction, animation, audio, online, testing,\nresearch, environment, model, usage), TESTING FEEDBACK, ENGINE FEEDBACK, PROMPT FEEDBACK (the answers to TASK.md's\nquestions, written by the builders at the end), CREDITS (my-3D2dge v0.85.2 by Michael Crosato, MIT; Kenney asset\nentries used, CC0; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; \"all music, sounds and voices synthesized in code\"; the cast).\nThe same text goes in the final chat reply and in `exit-interview.json` (Appendix E).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Content\n\n### 6.1 Hunts and maps\n\n| Hunt | Species | Time and weather | Host / rival | Map (1024 m core) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Hollow Creek** | whitetail deer | autumn morning, valley mist, falling leaves | Uncle Dub; Granny Mae hosts the bonus | rolling hardwood hills; a creek meanders north to south; Granny Mae's farm (red barn, cornfield, pasture, fences) in the south-east; a hardwood ridge in the west; Fog Glade, a clearing in the north-west |\n| **Bugle Ridge** | elk | alpine dusk, sun behind the peaks | Loretta at the trap house | a high meadow ringed by aspens; a valley with a talus slope opposite; a timberline saddle to the west; a lake below; peaks in the Backdrop |\n| **Muskeg Lake** | moose | first snow, overcast, fog banks | Big Earl by the lake fire | a lake with reed shallows and a beaver lodge; spruce bog to the north; a burned clearing with charred snags to the east; a snowy shore |\n\nVantages per hunt (positions in metres in the core; authored with the dev free camera): three site vantages, the\ntrophy vantage and the bonus vantage, linked by trail paths for the walk-ins.\n\n### 6.2 Sites\n\n| Site | Vantage | FOV | Distances | Bucks | Time | Spawns (outline) | Critters |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Hollow 1 **Creek Crossing** | tree stand 4.5 m up over a ford | 34° | 18-50 m | 3 | 60 s | a doe and fawn cross first; a 6-pointer grazes on the bank, drinks; two bucks bound across the ford with a doe between them | squirrel on an oak (50), rabbit (75) |\n| Hollow 2 **Cornfield Edge** | ground blind at the field corner | 28° | 30-90 m | 4 | 70 s | pairs burst out of the corn rows (emerge), run the fence line; one jumps the fence; a 10-pointer last | turkeys x3 (150), skunk (-100), Bessie the cow (-500) |\n| Hollow 3 **Hardwood Ridge** | rock outcrop on the ridge | 32° | 25-70 m | 4 | 75 s | deer weave between trunks (wait for gaps); a buck bedded behind a log bolts at the first shot; a decoy doe | raccoon in a log (100), squirrels (50) |\n| Bugle 1 **Aspen Park** | knoll above the meadow | 28° | 40-80 m | 3 | 75 s | a herd of 8 cows with 2 bulls grazes; a satellite bull bugles in the aspens and steps out when called | marmot (75), grouse flush (150), eagle (-400) |\n| Bugle 2 **Talus Slope** | across the valley | 22° | 100-180 m | 3 | 75 s | elk traverse the far slope (scope and hold breath); rockfall startles them | coyote on the ridge (250) |\n| Bugle 3 **Timberline Saddle** | facing the sunset | 26° | 50-90 m | 4 | 70 s | groups cross the saddle as backlit silhouettes; a bull charges downhill toward you, then veers | grouse (150), marmot (75) |\n| Muskeg 1 **Reed Shallows** | a canoe offshore (bobbing) | 30° | 35-80 m | 2 (+3 cows, a calf) | 70 s | moose wade through reeds (legs below the water); a cow and calf cross close | ducks (150), beaver (100), loons (-400) |\n| Muskeg 2 **Spruce Bog** | a bog edge in fog | 36° | 20-50 m | 3 | 70 s | fog banks drift; moose loom out close; one stands and stares instead of running | snowshoe hare (125), raven (100) |\n| Muskeg 3 **Burn Clearing** | a snowy rise over the burn | 26° | 50-110 m | 3 | 75 s | moose trot across; two bulls lock antlers (fight) then split; a wolf pack chases a cow through (don't hit her) | wolves x3 (300), raven (100) |\n\nFOV is the vertical field of view in degrees, telephoto-ish so animals read at 480 x 270: at 28° a whitetail (head\nup, about 23 units tall before the `animalScale` boost) is about 26 px tall at 30 m, 16 px at 50 m and 10 px at 80 m,\nwhere the scope (x3.5) makes it 34 px. Keep most shots inside 90 m; longer ones are scope shots by design.\n\n### 6.3 Trophies\n\n| Trophy | Where | Rules |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Old Iron Rack** (14-point whitetail) | Fog Glade at dawn, 60-100 m, 45 s | appears in 3 windows of 3.5 s between fog banks; a doe walks in front of him in window 3; he ignores calls until window 3 (then freezes 1.0 s) |\n| **The Duke of Bugle Ridge** (7 x 7 bull elk) | dark timber edge, 70-120 m, 50 s | he bugles from the trees (panned left or right so you can hear where); each of your calls draws him to the next opening for 4 s (4 openings); a cow leads him through the second; calling a fifth time sends him off |\n| **Big Mo** (72-inch bull moose) | the lake shore, 110 m in to 20 m, 45 s | bursts from the reeds and charges the stand over about 8 s; a lethal hit drops him; a gut or ham hit slows him; at 15 m he flattens the stand (screen tilt and crash: BIG MO SAYS NO!) and the trophy is lost; if missed he retreats and charges again, three times |\n\n### 6.4 Bonus games (30 s each)\n\n| Bonus | Host | Targets and rules |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Crow Patrol** (Hollow) | Granny Mae on her porch | crows flap up from Granny's corn in bursts, swoop and land on Hank the scarecrow: crows 100, the golden crow 500; hitting Hank -250 (\"Hank's got feelin's!\"); 10 rounds, rack 0.15 s |\n| **Saucer Season** (Bugle) | Loretta at the trap house | clay saucers from the trap: singles, doubles, crossing pairs, a high tower; 75 each, golden clay 500; 12 rounds |\n| **Snowball Standoff** (Muskeg) | Big Earl | snowmen pop up behind drifts and lob snowballs at you: shoot snowballs in the air (75) and knock hats off (150); a snowball that lands splats over part of the screen for 2 s; at 20 s the Snowmoose rises (a giant snow moose: its top hat 1000); 12 rounds |\n\nEach has a PERFECT bonus (every target hit, no misses: the bonus total doubles) and its own high-score table.\n\n### 6.5 Practice Range (Uncle Dub's)\nA flat field with berms and paper targets (custom props whose hit zones are flat rings), 7 stations, each a short line\nfrom Dub, an objective, and a check:\n1. **Aim and fire**: three paper bucks at 20 m.\n2. **Pump**: fire, pump, fire; then empty the tube and reload.\n3. **Shot placement**: a paper buck with the vital ring: put one in the heart (the zone callout shows).\n4. **Bucks only**: a moving target track alternating paper bucks and does: shoot only bucks (a doe hit is explained,\n   not punished).\n5. **Scope and breath**: a 150 m target: hold the scope, hold breath, fire (each named by its glyph).\n6. **The call**: a mechanical deer runs a rail; call to stop it, then shoot.\n7. **Critters**: tin squirrels pop up; a tin skunk with a DON'T sign.\nThen \"You'll do. Go win that Hunt-Off.\" and the Range badge in the Lodge. Prompts always use the last device's glyphs.\n\n### 6.6 Species (gameplay numbers)\n\n| Species | Target / protected | Shoulder, length | Walk / trot / run (m/s) | Antlers | hp | Points |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| whitetail | buck / doe, fawn | 1.0 m, 1.8 m | 1.3 / 3.4 / 8.5 | 4-12 points; trophy 14 | 1 | 100 + 15/point |\n| elk | bull / cow, calf | 1.5 m, 2.4 m | 1.4 / 4.0 / 9.0 | 5x5 to 6x6; trophy 7x7 | 1.5 | 150 + 20/point |\n| moose | bull / cow, calf | 1.9 m, 2.9 m | 1.5 / 4.5 / 8.0 (charge 9.5) | 40-55 in spread; trophy 72 in | 2 | 200 + 6/inch |\n\n### 6.7 Critters (12 designs)\n\n| Critter | Rig | Behaviour | Points | Hunts |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| squirrel | Blob (cat ears, bushy tail, feet) | climbs a trunk, runs a log, chatters | 50 | Hollow |\n| rabbit / snowshoe hare | Blob (rabbit ears, feet) | hops in arcs, freezes, bolts (hare is white) | 75 / 125 | Hollow / Muskeg |\n| wild turkey | Blob + fan and wattle | struts, gobbles, runs, flushes | 150 | Hollow |\n| raccoon | Blob + mask, ringed tail | peeks from a hollow log, ducks back | 100 | Hollow |\n| skunk (protected) | Blob + stripe | waddles; if shot: stink cloud | -100 | Hollow |\n| Bessie the cow (protected) | Quadruped cow | grazes in the pasture, moos | -500 | Hollow |\n| crow / raven | Blob bird | flies over in loose flocks, caws | 100 | Hollow bonus / Muskeg |\n| grouse | Blob bird | flushes from cover with a whirr, flies low | 150 | Bugle |\n| marmot | Blob | pops up on rocks, whistles, ducks | 75 | Bugle |\n| coyote / wolf | Quadruped canid | trots the ridge, howls; wolves chase in a pack | 250 / 300 | Bugle / Muskeg |\n| eagle (protected) | Blob bird, big | soars in circles high up | -400 | Bugle |\n| duck / loon (protected) / beaver | Blob bird; Blob swimmer | ducks flush and fly; loons float and wail; the beaver swims with a wake and slaps | 150 / -400 / 100 | Muskeg |\n\n### 6.8 Cast and story beats\n\n**Cast**: the Emcee (announcer of the Hunt-Off), Uncle Dub (your guide), Granny Mae (farm owner, Crow Patrol host),\nCousin Dwayne (rival, boastful), Loretta Pruitt (rival, sharp and kind), Big Earl (rival, here for the chili).\n\n| Beat | When | Lines (write more in the same voice; keep each under about 60 characters) |\n|---|---|---|\n| welcome | first Hunt-Off start | EMCEE: \"Welcome to the 41st Annual Big Buck Hunt-Off!\" / EMCEE: \"Three hunts. One trophy wall. Zero does!\" / DUB: \"Name's Dub. Forty years guidin'. Lost twice. On purpose.\" |\n| rivals | after welcome | DWAYNE: \"Hope you packed a lunch, cuz. You'll be here a while.\" / LORETTA: \"Ignore him. He shot a mailbox in '09.\" / EARL: \"I'm mostly here for the chili.\" |\n| hollow intro | Hollow Creek start | DUB: \"Whitetails thick as ticks out here.\" / DUB: \"Bucks got antlers. Does don't. Can't tell? Don't pull.\" / DUB: \"Pump after every shot. This rifle's older'n me.\" |\n| iron rack legend | before the trophy | DUB: \"Old Iron Rack. Fourteen points.\" / DUB: \"Walks in the fog so nobody can count 'em.\" / DUB: \"Been dodgin' hunters since your daddy wore diapers.\" |\n| crow patrol | before the bonus | GRANNY: \"Crows ate my sweet corn. Every last ear!\" / GRANNY: \"Shoot the crows, sugar. Not Hank.\" |\n| hollow outro | after results | DWAYNE (behind): \"Scope's crooked. That's all that is.\" or DWAYNE (ahead): \"Told ya. Bring a lunch.\" |\n| bugle intro | Bugle Ridge start | DUB: \"Elk hear a bugle, they come lookin' for a fight.\" / DUB: \"Give 'em a call and they'll stop to see who's talkin'.\" |\n| duke legend | before the trophy | DUB: \"The Duke don't come out for just anybody.\" / DUB: \"Answer him back. Make him curious.\" |\n| saucer season | before the bonus | LORETTA: \"Pull!... That's what you say. Then you shoot it.\" |\n| muskeg intro | Muskeg Lake start | DUB: \"Moose ain't skittish. Moose is a truck with opinions.\" / EARL: \"Chili's on the fire if you live.\" |\n| big mo legend | before the trophy | DUB: \"Big Mo don't run from you.\" / DUB: \"He runs AT you. Hold steady.\" |\n| snowball standoff | before the bonus | EARL: \"The snowmen are back. They want revenge.\" |\n| ceremony | after Muskeg results | EMCEE: placement line (\"Our new Hunt-Off champion!\" / \"There's always next year!\"), DUB: \"Hang it on the wall, kid.\" Then the Lodge with the new mounts, then the credits page |\n\n### 6.9 Barks (emcee unless noted)\n\n| Category | Lines |\n|---|---|\n| start | BUCKS ONLY! / HERE THEY COME! / EYES SHARP, HUNTERS! / THREE BUCKS ON THE MOVE! (count from the site) |\n| kill | NICE SHOT! / BAGGED 'EM! / WHAT A SHOT! / DOWN HE GOES! |\n| zones | HEART SHOT! / HEADSHOT! / LUNG SHOT! / NECK SHOT! / SHOULDER! / GUT SHOT... FINISH HIM! |\n| long / running / quick | LONG SHOT! CALL THE PAPER! / RUNNING SHOT! / QUICK DRAW! |\n| multi | DOUBLE! / TRIPLE! THE CROWD GOES MILD! |\n| miss | MISSED HIM CLEAN! / THAT'S A LOT OF DIRT YOU KILLED! / BARK'S DEAD, BUCK AIN'T! |\n| pump / reload | PUMP IT! / RELOAD, HOSS! |\n| doe | DOE! YOU'RE OUT! / THAT'S A DOE! HOLSTER UP! / AW, NOT MAMA! / A FAWN?! GO SIT IN THE TRUCK! |\n| protected | OH, THE STINK! / THAT'S BESSIE!! / THAT'S THE NATIONAL BIRD, BUDDY! / NOT THE LOON! |\n| escape / lost | HE'S GETTIN' AWAY! / GONE LIKE A RUMOR! / WOUNDED AND LOST... |\n| trophy | TROPHY SPOTTED! / THAT'S OLD IRON RACK! / THE DUKE! / HERE COMES BIG MO! / TROPHY BAGGED! / THE ONE THAT GOT AWAY... |\n| end | SITE CLEAR! / TIME! / CLEAN SWEEP! |\n| critters | CRITTER BONUS! / SQUIRREL! / TURKEY DINNER! |\n| Dub (tips, quieter) | \"Wait for him to clear that tree.\" / \"Hold your breath. Steady as a church pew.\" / \"Give him a grunt.\" |\n\n### 6.10 Items and unlockables\nThere are no pickups or power-ups in play; the player's kit and the goals are:\n- **The kit**: the pump rifle (5-round tube), the scope, and a call per hunt (a grunt tube at Hollow Creek, a bugle at\n  Bugle Ridge, a moose call at Muskeg Lake), introduced by Dub in each hunt's briefing with its glyph.\n- **Special targets** that play the power-up role: the golden crow, the golden clay, the Snowmoose's hat; quick-draw,\n  long-shot and multi-kill bonuses.\n- **Unlockables kept in the Lodge**: the three trophy mounts, each hunt's best-buck plaque, stars per site (27 in all),\n  the Range badge, the Hunt-Off champion plaque (first place in the campaign), high-score entries with initials.\n- Everything is playable from the start (no locked hunts): the demo must show all of it.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Build order and milestones\n\nBuild the spine first, one hunt to a full vertical slice, then widen. Each milestone ends with its tests passing\n(`node tests/run.mjs`) and, where it says so, screenshots looked at.\n\n| # | Milestone | Delivers | Done when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| M0 | Setup | dev folder, engine and hub copies, manifest, build script, dev page, test runner and headless loader, `game.debug` stub with snapshot | `node tests/run.mjs` runs (one smoke test); the bundle opens from `file://` with no errors |\n| M1 | Gallery on a flat floor | E.Lens, Vista with flat terrain, Backdrop sky, billboards with impostors (library trees and rocks), static deer silhouettes, P1 reticle (mouse and pad), fire with analytic sphere hits, a minimal HUD | shooting a silhouette works by mouse and pad; lens tests pass; screenshot looks like a pixel landscape |\n| M2 | The deer | E.Quadruped whitetail (skeleton, 4 gaits, poses, antlers, outline, LOD, zones, x-ray, mount), Animal Lab | quadruped tests pass; filmstrips of every gait and the death look right |\n| M3 | The land | E.Heightfield (base, features, water, ground types, light bake, scatter, occluders), terrain raster with occlusion, water, fog and mist, Hollow Creek map, custom props (corn, reeds, tall grass, birch, barn, stand, blind) | terrain and occlusion tests pass; Hollow's three vantages screenshot well; animals hide behind crests |\n| M4 | Shooting for real | rifle (pump, tube, reload), scope lens with sway and breath, call, aim assist, full shot resolution with zones, occluders, terrain and water, impacts and particles, scoring v1, banners and pops | weapon, aim, shot and score tests pass; pick-agreement check at 95% |","numLines":450,"startLine":800,"totalLines":1563}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SH7UB8T5GyGhjPtrVms1ow","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
