{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A6j1Etrx1zum2NcdbuYvfF","type":"tool_result","content":"136:- `E.bayer(x, y)` †: the 4 x 4 ordered-dither threshold 0..1 at pixel (x, y): pixel on when value > bayer(x, y)\n139:- `E.ctx2d(c)`: a canvas's 2D context with smoothing off (crisp pixels)\n163:- `E.hex(h)`: '#rrggbb' or '#rgb' (or an [r, g, b] array) -> [r, g, b]\n169:- `E.mix(h1, h2, t)`: the color t of the way from h1 to h2 ('#rrggbb')\n170:- `E.mkCanvas(w, h)`: a new canvas of w x h pixels (scratch images and sprite sheets). With no document (Node: a headless game) a stand-in whose drawing does nothing, so sprites and other images made while a game loads don't stop it\n171:- `E.noise2(x, y)`: smooth value noise 0..1 over the plane (one bump per whole unit): blotches, clouds, wobble\n176:- `E.ramp(c, n = 5, strength = 1)`: a ramp of n colors from dark to light around a base color (hue shifted), for palettes and gradients\n179:- `E.rng(s)`: a seeded random stream: const R = E.rng(42); R() gives 0..1, the same numbers for the same seed (mulberry32)\n181:- `E.shade(h, a)`: shade('#336699', -0.3) darker, (+0.3) lighter. Hue-shifted like painted pixel art: darker drifts cool, lighter drifts warm\n190:- `E.tones(c, strength = 1)`: five shades of a color for painted-looking pixel art: { deep, sh, base, lt, hi }. Shadows drift toward blue-violet, highlights toward warm yellow (strength 0..2, default 1).\n490:- `game.players` †: the players: [game.input (player 1), ...the ones who joined (game.allowJoin, game.addPlayer: section 10j)]; each an input with player (1..4), name ('P1'), color (E.PLAYER_COLORS) and device. A game of one: [game.input]\n559:- `E.PLAYER_COLORS: #4a8aff, #ff4a4a, #4ad860, #ffd040` †: the players' colors: player 1 blue, 2 red, 3 green, 4 yellow (game.players)\n197:- `px.blend(g, a, mode, fn)`: draw fn() at alpha a (stepped, like PS1 hardware) with a blend mode: 'normal', 'add', 'multiply', 'screen' (E.style.trans = 'dither' dithers instead)\n198:- `px.col(g, c)`: set the fill color (px.* do it themselves)\n199:- `px.ddisc(g, cx, cy, r, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: soft disc that fades toward its edge (glows, smoke, dust): stepped alpha rings, or dithering in 'dither' style\n200:- `px.disc(g, cx, cy, r, c)`: a filled circle\n201:- `px.dot(g, x, y, c)`: one pixel\n202:- `px.ell(g, cx, cy, rx, ry, c)`: a filled ellipse\n203:- `px.glow(g, e = 1)`: GPU lighting: what follows glows (0..1). No effect in Canvas mode, so call it freely.\n204:- `px.line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, w = 1)`: a line w pixels thick, no smoothing\n205:- `px.poly(g, pts, c)`: a filled polygon through [[x, y], ...]\n206:- `px.polyDither(g, pts, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: translucent polygon: a = 0..1 opacity (stepped alpha, or a dither pattern in 'dither' style). wx/wy = world pixel offset for the pattern\n207:- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`: a filled rectangle, snapped to whole pixels\n208:- `px.reset(g)`: forget the color cache (after drawing on g with the canvas API directly)\n209:- `px.sprite(g, spr, x, y, flip = false)`: draw a sprite with its top-left corner at buffer pixel (x, y). flip mirrors it left-right; or o: { flip, rot (radians, turned about its center: E.rotSpri","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3fa61e8-1431-4900-ae89-edc59162574b","uuid":"ed289dd4-2607-428b-88ba-eb241647c7c8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:09:07.197Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"136:- `E.bayer(x, y)` †: the 4 x 4 ordered-dither threshold 0..1 at pixel (x, y): pixel on when value > bayer(x, y)\n139:- `E.ctx2d(c)`: a canvas's 2D context with smoothing off (crisp pixels)\n163:- `E.hex(h)`: '#rrggbb' or '#rgb' (or an [r, g, b] array) -> [r, g, b]\n169:- `E.mix(h1, h2, t)`: the color t of the way from h1 to h2 ('#rrggbb')\n170:- `E.mkCanvas(w, h)`: a new canvas of w x h pixels (scratch images and sprite sheets). With no document (Node: a headless game) a stand-in whose drawing does nothing, so sprites and other images made wh