{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghxREQiTQ93sKwUSS6Vz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VmeDPi5mtY1MwChdbTHYxY","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050554__x4cdb93/work/BigBuckHuntOff-BigBuckHunterPro-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-050554/build/report.json","content":"{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:05:54\",\n    \"source\": \"Big Buck Hunter Pro (arcade, 2006; designed by Play Mechanix, made and distributed by Raw Thrills)\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Arcade light-gun hunting shooter (a shooting gallery in a living landscape) with party versus, trophy encounters and bonus mini-games\",\n    \"perspective\": \"First person on rails: a fixed vantage per site with scripted camera pans over a pseudo-3D heightfield landscape; a slow-motion Trophy Cam; side-on x-ray Shot Charts; 2D menus and an engine side-view Lodge\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff package (full engine, lightly changed) plus about 4,800 lines of game code in vanilla JavaScript: an own software renderer on Canvas 2D (column-marched heightfield, depth buffer, shaded capsule pixel volumes), a procedural quadruped rig, Web Audio; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; tests on Node 24.22.1 and Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium (build 1243)\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's native retro-modern pixel style at 480x270 (E.tones shading with ordered dither, 1-pixel outlines, the 5x7 pixel font, E.font.title logos, E.ui windows, Humanoid portraits); new procedural deer, elk, moose, canids, the cow, critters, birds, antlers, trees, rocks, barn, blinds, canoe, scarecrow, snowmen and clays; three palettes: autumn morning, alpine dusk, first snow\",\n    \"animation\": \"Engine-native procedural animation posed by math every step: a new quadruped rig (walk, trot, gallop and bound gaits, graze, alert, look, call, hurt, limp, jump, death), small procedural critter and bird rigs (hops, flaps, peeks, struts), in-world capsule folk, and the engine's E.Humanoid and E.Blob in the Lodge and dialog portraits\",\n    \"audio\": \"All in code: bluegrass chiptune songs on the engine synth (title hoedown, lodge fire, stalking music with drum and tension layers, bonus jamboree, results, stings), layered sound effects (rifle crack with thump, tail and two valley echoes, pump, shells, calls, impacts, critters), ambience beds per hunt, and Animalese-style gibberish voices for six characters through formant filters\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1-4 players: the game's own card, a 3-minute Hub Hunt-Off keyed to the hub clock, ghost reticles and shots, progress every second, one result (also on time-up), round-over standings. The real harness passed with 2 players, with 4 players at latency 150 / jitter 50 / loss 5, and with host-leave\",\n    \"testing\": \"Allowed: unlimited headless testing with the engine's game.advance and game.debug, a scripted playthrough of the whole game, one command printing only failures and a count, screenshots only where scripts can't check, no subagent or workflow reviews. Ran: node tests/run.mjs, 210 headless checks in 7 suites (unit, sites, modes, playthrough of the whole Hunt-Off, attract/dev/saves/determinism, touch-only, AI Hub stub), all passing; --browser adds 22 Playwright checks (15 deep links with no errors, pick agreement, gamepad glyphs, the phone gate), all passing; the AI Hub harness in 3 scenarios, all passing; screenshots reviewed by eye\",\n    \"research\": \"None by the build stage beyond the plan's: the plan read Wikipedia's Big Buck Hunter article, the Highway Games cabinet listing and Macworld's iPhone review (other sites gave search summaries only); the build read the my-3D2dge handoff docs (README, API.md, the index) and the AI Hub lib/hub README and ghost example\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Playwright Chromium (headless shell, build 1243) for checks\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"Cost and token totals: unknown (no meter available in the session); session time about 1 hour 15 minutes (05:05 to about 06:20)\"\n  },\n  \"testingQuestions\": [\"How many issues did testing catch?\", \"How many were critical / game breaking?\", \"Most helpful test\", \"Least helpful test\"],\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"About 30: a coroutine infinite loop on zero-length waits (Big Mo's site hung), a 30x slowdown from running the engine in a vm sandbox, an int hash deopt, the creek carved into a 6 m gorge, overlapping site fans burying a vantage in a hillside, moose wading 2.5 m deep, reeds and corn blocking shots, the bot leading hitscan shots and locking on hidden targets, dry cells marked as water, animals spawning far outside the view, touch-only not clearing, the hub sending no ghosts during the opening pan, glyph keycaps unreadable, a listener crash on shot events, the lodge exit and several test-timing issues\",\n    \"Five would have broken the game: the coroutine hang (a frozen trophy), the gorge and hillside terrain (unplayable sites), the moose underwater (unwinnable site) and the missing ghost messages (the hub would reject the game)\",\n    \"The scripted playthrough of the whole Hunt-Off with the cheat bot, together with the per-site bot runs: they exercised every site, trophy, bonus, tally and results screen and found the hang and the unwinnable sites\",\n    \"The determinism hash check: it passed first time and caught nothing, though it guards the hub sync\"\n  ],\n  \"engineQuestions\": [\"What I liked most\", \"Stuck or guessed wrong\", \"Most important thing I built\", \"Hardest part\", \"What I changed in the engine, and why\", \"One thing I would change\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"The standard features: the pause menu, settings, rebinding, controls screen, glyph families, full screen and boot screen came free, and E.Dialog with live Humanoid portraits gave the cast a voice in minutes. game.advance made fast headless tests easy\",\n    \"Yes: the pixel helpers cache the fill colour, and the font's default outline flooded small keycaps; I first guessed the cache was the cause. I also guessed that loading the engine in a vm sandbox was fine; global lookups there were 30x slower\",\n    \"The Vista renderer: a column-marched heightfield with a depth buffer and shaded capsule pixel volumes, so terrain, trees, animals and the scope lens share one depth test, and shots hit exactly what is drawn\",\n    \"Fitting a first-person, perspective game into an engine whose views are orthographic: none of the world drawing (props, lights, particles, the camera) could be reused for the hunt itself, only the HUD, menus and the Lodge\",\n    \"Three small changes: the default button symbols are PlayStation (TASK.md asks for them; the Xbox option stays); audio.bus('sfx' | 'music') returns the bus node so the gibberish voices follow the effects volume and mute; the Input's default glyph family matches. Everything else lives in the game's own modules\",\n    \"A perspective (first-person or chase) view with a depth buffer in the 2D engine, so props, rigs and lights could be drawn into it\"\n  ],\n  \"promptQuestions\": [\"What I liked most\", \"What was confusing\", \"Hardest thing to do\", \"What I would change\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"A concrete plan to build from plus a clear definition of done, with testing rules that say exactly how to prove it works\",\n    \"The plan names a dev folder and file with 'max' and yesterday's timestamp, while TASK.md names 'medium' and today's; TASK.md wins, as STAGE.md says, but it took a moment to be sure\",\n    \"Getting a whole feature-complete arcade game (renderer, rigs, nine sites, three trophies, three bonus games, a range, party, attract, dev mode, AI Hub) built and verified in one session\",\n    \"Let the plan's file names be filled in by the build stage, and say up front how large a plan is (1,560 lines) so the build can budget its reading\"\n  ],\n  \"credits\": [[\"Game\", \"Big Buck Hunt-Off, an original game inspired by Big Buck Hunter Pro. No names, art, music or levels from the source\"], [\"Engine\", \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 by Michael Crosato (MIT), with a small change list in Engine Feedback\"], [\"Online\", \"AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (Session Protocol v1)\"], [\"Sound\", \"All music, sound effects and voices synthesized in code\"], [\"Cast\", \"The Emcee, Uncle Dub, Granny Mae, Cousin Dwayne, Loretta Pruitt, Big Earl, Hank the scarecrow, Bessie the cow\"], [\"Built by\", \"Anthropic claude-opus-5-5 (medium effort) in Claude Code, from PLAN.md\"]],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Big Buck Hunt-Off\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Bucks only. Bragging rights forever.\",\n    \"description\": \"An arcade light-gun hunting shooter in living pixel landscapes: bag the bucks, spare the does, and win the Hunt-Off alone, on the couch or online.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Shooter\",\n    \"source\": \"Big Buck Hunter Pro\",\n    \"series\": \"Big Buck Hunter\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Aim: mouse or left stick · Shoot: left click or R2 · Pump: R or Square · Scope: right click or L2 · Call: Q or Triangle\",\n    \"tags\": [\"first-person\", \"arcade\", \"pixel art\", \"versus\", \"comedy\", \"retro\"]\n  }\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":505,"cache_read_input_tokens":586327,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":505},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3fa61e8-1431-4900-ae89-edc59162574b","uuid":"845fa887-92e8-41cf-87ba-e5cc39f876c2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:20:55.193Z","request_id":"req_011CghxRDrEHNdNxnUFouAQT","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VmeDPi5mtY1MwChdbTHYxY":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050554__x4cdb93/work/BigBuckHuntOff-BigBuckHunterPro-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-050554/build/report.json","content":"{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:05:54\",\n    \"source\": \"Big Buck Hunter Pro (arcade, 2006; designed by Play Mechanix, made and distributed by Raw Thrills)\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Arcade light-gun hunting shooter (a shooting gallery in a living landscape) with party versus, trophy encounters and bonus mini-games\",\n    \"perspective\": \"First person on rails: a fixed vantage per site with scripted camera pans over a pseudo-3D heightfield landscape; a slow-motion Trophy Cam; side-on x-ray Shot Charts; 2D menus and an engine side-view Lodge\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff package (full engine, lightly changed) plus about 4,800 lines of game code in vanilla JavaScript: an own software renderer on Canvas 2D (column-marched heightfield, depth buffer, shaded capsule pixel volumes), a procedural quadruped rig, Web Audio; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; tests on Node 24.22.1 and Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium (build 1243)\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's native retro-modern pixel style at 480x270 (E.tones shading with ordered dither, 1-pixel outlines, the 5x7 pixel font, E.font.title logos, E.ui windows, Humanoid portraits); new procedural deer, elk, moose, canids, the cow, critters, birds, antlers, trees, rocks, barn, blinds, canoe, scarecrow, snowmen and clays; three palettes: autumn morning, alpine dusk, first snow\",\n    \"animation\": \"Engine-native procedural animation posed by math every step: a new quadruped rig (walk, trot, gallop and bound gaits, graze, alert, look, call, hurt, limp, jump, death), small procedural critter and bird rigs (hops, flaps, peeks, struts), in-world capsule folk, and the engine's E.Humanoid and E.Blob in the Lodge and dialog portraits\",\n    \"audio\": \"All in code: bluegrass chiptune songs on the engine synth (title hoedown, lodge fire, stalking music with drum and tension layers, bonus jamboree, results, stings), layered sound effects (rifle crack with thump, tail and two valley echoes, pump, shells, calls, impacts, critters), ambience beds per hunt, and Animalese-style gibberish voices for six characters through formant filters\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1-4 players: the game's own card, a 3-minute Hub Hunt-Off keyed to the hub clock, ghost reticles and shots, progress every second, one result (also on time-up), round-over standings. The real harness passed with 2 players, with 4 players at latency 150 / jitter 50 / loss 5, and with host-leave\",\n    \"testing\": \"Allowed: unlimited headless testing with the engine's game.advance and game.debug, a scripted playthrough of the whole game, one command printing only failures and a count, screenshots only where scripts can't check, no subagent or workflow reviews. Ran: node tests/run.mjs, 210 headless checks in 7 suites (unit, sites, modes, playthrough of the whole Hunt-Off, attract/dev/saves/determinism, touch-only, AI Hub stub), all passing; --browser adds 22 Playwright checks (15 deep links with no errors, pick agreement, gamepad glyphs, the phone gate), all passing; the AI Hub harness in 3 scenarios, all passing; screenshots reviewed by eye\",\n    \"research\": \"None by the build stage beyond the plan's: the plan read Wikipedia's Big Buck Hunter article, the Highway Games cabinet listing and Macworld's iPhone review (other sites gave search summaries only); the build read the my-3D2dge handoff docs (README, API.md, the index) and the AI Hub lib/hub README and ghost example\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Playwright Chromium (headless shell, build 1243) for checks\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"Cost and token totals: unknown (no meter available in the session); session time about 1 hour 15 minutes (05:05 to about 06:20)\"\n  },\n  \"testingQuestions\": [\"How many issues did testing catch?\", \"How many were critical / game breaking?\", \"Most helpful test\", \"Least helpful test\"],\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"About 30: a coroutine infinite loop on zero-length waits (Big Mo's site hung), a 30x slowdown from running the engine in a vm sandbox, an int hash deopt, the creek carved into a 6 m gorge, overlapping site fans burying a vantage in a hillside, moose wading 2.5 m deep, reeds and corn blocking shots, the bot leading hitscan shots and locking on hidden targets, dry cells marked as water, animals spawning far outside the view, touch-only not clearing, the hub sending no ghosts during the opening pan, glyph keycaps unreadable, a listener crash on shot events, the lodge exit and several test-timing issues\",\n    \"Five would have broken the game: the coroutine hang (a frozen trophy), the gorge and hillside terrain (unplayable sites), the moose underwater (unwinnable site) and the missing ghost messages (the hub would reject the game)\",\n    \"The scripted playthrough of the whole Hunt-Off with the cheat bot, together with the per-site bot runs: they exercised every site, trophy, bonus, tally and results screen and found the hang and the unwinnable sites\",\n    \"The determinism hash check: it passed first time and caught nothing, though it guards the hub sync\"\n  ],\n  \"engineQuestions\": [\"What I liked most\", \"Stuck or guessed wrong\", \"Most important thing I built\", \"Hardest part\", \"What I changed in the engine, and why\", \"One thing I would change\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"The standard features: the pause menu, settings, rebinding, controls screen, glyph families, full screen and boot screen came free, and E.Dialog with live Humanoid portraits gave the cast a voice in minutes. game.advance made fast headless tests easy\",\n    \"Yes: the pixel helpers cache the fill colour, and the font's default outline flooded small keycaps; I first guessed the cache was the cause. I also guessed that loading the engine in a vm sandbox was fine; global lookups there were 30x slower\",\n    \"The Vista renderer: a column-marched heightfield with a depth buffer and shaded capsule pixel volumes, so terrain, trees, animals and the scope lens share one depth test, and shots hit exactly what is drawn\",\n    \"Fitting a first-person, perspective game into an engine whose views are orthographic: none of the world drawing (props, lights, particles, the camera) could be reused for the hunt itself, only the HUD, menus and the Lodge\",\n    \"Three small changes: the default button symbols are PlayStation (TASK.md asks for them; the Xbox option stays); audio.bus('sfx' | 'music') returns the bus node so the gibberish voices follow the effects volume and mute; the Input's default glyph family matches. Everything else lives in the game's own modules\",\n    \"A perspective (first-person or chase) view with a depth buffer in the 2D engine, so props, rigs and lights could be drawn into it\"\n  ],\n  \"promptQuestions\": [\"What I liked most\", \"What was confusing\", \"Hardest thing to do\", \"What I would change\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"A concrete plan to build from plus a clear definition of done, with testing rules that say exactly how to prove it works\",\n    \"The plan names a dev folder and file with 'max' and yesterday's timestamp, while TASK.md names 'medium' and today's; TASK.md wins, as STAGE.md says, but it took a moment to be sure\",\n    \"Getting a whole feature-complete arcade game (renderer, rigs, nine sites, three trophies, three bonus games, a range, party, attract, dev mode, AI Hub) built and verified in one session\",\n    \"Let the plan's file names be filled in by the build stage, and say up front how large a plan is (1,560 lines) so the build can budget its reading\"\n  ],\n  \"credits\": [[\"Game\", \"Big Buck Hunt-Off, an original game inspired by Big Buck Hunter Pro. No names, art, music or levels from the source\"], [\"Engine\", \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 by Michael Crosato (MIT), with a small change list in Engine Feedback\"], [\"Online\", \"AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (Session Protocol v1)\"], [\"Sound\", \"All music, sound effects and voices synthesized in code\"], [\"Cast\", \"The Emcee, Uncle Dub, Granny Mae, Cousin Dwayne, Loretta Pruitt, Big Earl, Hank the scarecrow, Bessie the cow\"], [\"Built by\", \"Anthropic claude-opus-5-5 (medium effort) in Claude Code, from PLAN.md\"]],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Big Buck Hunt-Off\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Bucks only. Bragging rights forever.\",\n    \"description\": \"An arcade light-gun hunting shooter in living pixel landscapes: bag the bucks, spare the does, and win the Hunt-Off alone, on the couch or online.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Shooter\",\n    \"source\": \"Big Buck Hunter Pro\",\n    \"series\": \"Big Buck Hunter\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Aim: mouse or left stick · Shoot: left click or R2 · Pump: R or Square · Scope: right click or L2 · Call: Q or Triangle\",\n    \"tags\": [\"first-person\", \"arcade\", \"pixel art\", \"versus\", \"comedy\", \"retro\"]\n  }\n}\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VmeDPi5mtY1MwChdbTHYxY","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050554__x4cdb93/work/BigBuckHuntOff-BigBuckHunterPro-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-050554/build/report.json has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3fa61e8-1431-4900-ae89-edc59162574b","uuid":"c8691862-9358-44bf-b3b5-c911bad002eb","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:20:55.219Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050554__x4cdb93/work/BigBuckHuntOff-BigBuckHunterPro-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-050554/build/report.json","content":"{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:05:54\",\n    \"source\": \"Big Buck Hunter Pro (arcade, 2006; designed by Play Mechanix, made and distributed by Raw Thrills)\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Arcade light-gun hunting shooter (a shooting gallery in a living landscape) with party versus, trophy encounters and bonus mini-games\",\n    \"perspective\": \"First person on rails: a fixed vantage per site with scripted camera pans over a pseudo-3D heightfield landscape; a slow-motion Trophy Cam; side-on x-ray Shot Charts; 2D menus and an engine side-view Lodge\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff package (full engine, lightly changed) plus about 4,800 lines of game code in vanilla JavaScript: an own software renderer on Canvas 2D (column-marched heightfield, depth buffer, shaded capsule pixel volumes), a procedural quadruped rig, Web Audio; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; tests on Node 24.22.1 and Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium (build 1243)\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's native retro-modern pixel style at 480x270 (E.tones shading with ordered dither, 1-pixel outlines, the 5x7 pixel font, E.font.title logos, E.ui windows, Humanoid portraits); new procedural deer, elk, moose, canids, the cow, critters, birds, antlers, trees, rocks, barn, blinds, canoe, scarecrow, snowmen and clays; three palettes: autumn morning, alpine dusk, first snow\",\n    \"animation\": \"Engine-native procedural animation posed by math every step: a new quadruped rig (walk, trot, gallop and bound gaits, graze, alert, look, call, hurt, limp, jump, death), small procedural critter and bird rigs (hops, flaps, peeks, struts), in-world capsule folk, and the engine's E.Humanoid and E.Blob in the Lodge and dialog portraits\",\n    \"audio\": \"All in code: bluegrass chiptune songs on the engine synth (title hoedown, lodge fire, stalking music with drum and tension layers, bonus jamboree, results, stings), layered sound effects (rifle crack with thump, tail and two valley echoes, pump, shells, calls, impacts, critters), ambience beds per hunt, and Animalese-style gibberish voices for six characters through formant filters\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1-4 players: the game's own card, a 3-minute Hub Hunt-Off keyed to the hub clock, ghost reticles and shots, progress every second, one result (also on time-up), round-over standings. The real harness passed with 2 players, with 4 players at latency 150 / jitter 50 / loss 5, and with host-leave\",\n    \"testing\": \"Allowed: unlimited headless testing with the engine's game.advance and game.debug, a scripted playthrough of the whole game, one command printing only failures and a count, screenshots only where scripts can't check, no subagent or workflow reviews. Ran: node tests/run.mjs, 210 headless checks in 7 suites (unit, sites, modes, playthrough of the whole Hunt-Off, attract/dev/saves/determinism, touch-only, AI Hub stub), all passing; --browser adds 22 Playwright checks (15 deep links with no errors, pick agreement, gamepad glyphs, the phone gate), all passing; the AI Hub harness in 3 scenarios, all passing; screenshots reviewed by eye\",\n    \"research\": \"None by the build stage beyond the plan's: the plan read Wikipedia's Big Buck Hunter article, the Highway Games cabinet listing and Macworld's iPhone review (other sites gave search summaries only); the build read the my-3D2dge handoff docs (README, API.md, the index) and the AI Hub lib/hub README and ghost example\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Playwright Chromium (headless shell, build 1243) for checks\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"Cost and token totals: unknown (no meter available in the session); session time about 1 hour 15 minutes (05:05 to about 06:20)\"\n  },\n  \"testingQuestions\": [\"How many issues did testing catch?\", \"How many were critical / game breaking?\", \"Most helpful test\", \"Least helpful test\"],\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"About 30: a coroutine infinite loop on zero-length waits (Big Mo's site hung), a 30x slowdown from running the engine in a vm sandbox, an int hash deopt, the creek carved into a 6 m gorge, overlapping site fans burying a vantage in a hillside, moose wading 2.5 m deep, reeds and corn blocking shots, the bot leading hitscan shots and locking on hidden targets, dry cells marked as water, animals spawning far outside the view, touch-only not clearing, the hub sending no ghosts during the opening pan, glyph keycaps unreadable, a listener crash on shot events, the lodge exit and several test-timing issues\",\n    \"Five would have broken the game: the coroutine hang (a frozen trophy), the gorge and hillside terrain (unplayable sites), the moose underwater (unwinnable site) and the missing ghost messages (the hub would reject the game)\",\n    \"The scripted playthrough of the whole Hunt-Off with the cheat bot, together with the per-site bot runs: they exercised every site, trophy, bonus, tally and results screen and found the hang and the unwinnable sites\",\n    \"The determinism hash check: it passed first time and caught nothing, though it guards the hub sync\"\n  ],\n  \"engineQuestions\": [\"What I liked most\", \"Stuck or guessed wrong\", \"Most important thing I built\", \"Hardest part\", \"What I changed in the engine, and why\", \"One thing I would change\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"The standard features: the pause menu, settings, rebinding, controls screen, glyph families, full screen and boot screen came free, and E.Dialog with live Humanoid portraits gave the cast a voice in minutes. game.advance made fast headless tests easy\",\n    \"Yes: the pixel helpers cache the fill colour, and the font's default outline flooded small keycaps; I first guessed the cache was the cause. I also guessed that loading the engine in a vm sandbox was fine; global lookups there were 30x slower\",\n    \"The Vista renderer: a column-marched heightfield with a depth buffer and shaded capsule pixel volumes, so terrain, trees, animals and the scope lens share one depth test, and shots hit exactly what is drawn\",\n    \"Fitting a first-person, perspective game into an engine whose views are orthographic: none of the world drawing (props, lights, particles, the camera) could be reused for the hunt itself, only the HUD, menus and the Lodge\",\n    \"Three small changes: the default button symbols are PlayStation (TASK.md asks for them; the Xbox option stays); audio.bus('sfx' | 'music') returns the bus node so the gibberish voices follow the effects volume and mute; the Input's default glyph family matches. Everything else lives in the game's own modules\",\n    \"A perspective (first-person or chase) view with a depth buffer in the 2D engine, so props, rigs and lights could be drawn into it\"\n  ],\n  \"promptQuestions\": [\"What I liked most\", \"What was confusing\", \"Hardest thing to do\", \"What I would change\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"A concrete plan to build from plus a clear definition of done, with testing rules that say exactly how to prove it works\",\n    \"The plan names a dev folder and file with 'max' and yesterday's timestamp, while TASK.md names 'medium' and today's; TASK.md wins, as STAGE.md says, but it took a moment to be sure\",\n    \"Getting a whole feature-complete arcade game (renderer, rigs, nine sites, three trophies, three bonus games, a range, party, attract, dev mode, AI Hub) built and verified in one session\",\n    \"Let the plan's file names be filled in by the build stage, and say up front how large a plan is (1,560 lines) so the build can budget its reading\"\n  ],\n  \"credits\": [[\"Game\", \"Big Buck Hunt-Off, an original game inspired by Big Buck Hunter Pro. No names, art, music or levels from the source\"], [\"Engine\", \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 by Michael Crosato (MIT), with a small change list in Engine Feedback\"], [\"Online\", \"AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (Session Protocol v1)\"], [\"Sound\", \"All music, sound effects and voices synthesized in code\"], [\"Cast\", \"The Emcee, Uncle Dub, Granny Mae, Cousin Dwayne, Loretta Pruitt, Big Earl, Hank the scarecrow, Bessie the cow\"], [\"Built by\", \"Anthropic claude-opus-5-5 (medium effort) in Claude Code, from PLAN.md\"]],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Big Buck Hunt-Off\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Bucks only. Bragging rights forever.\",\n    \"description\": \"An arcade light-gun hunting shooter in living pixel landscapes: bag the bucks, spare the does, and win the Hunt-Off alone, on the couch or online.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Shooter\",\n    \"source\": \"Big Buck Hunter Pro\",\n    \"series\": \"Big Buck Hunter\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Aim: mouse or left stick · Shoot: left click or R2 · Pump: R or Square · Scope: right click or L2 · Call: Q or Triangle\",\n    \"tags\": [\"first-person\", \"arcade\", \"pixel art\", \"versus\", \"comedy\", \"retro\"]\n  }\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":3,"oldLines":26,"newStart":3,"newLines":43,"lines":["     \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:05:54\",","     \"source\": \"Big Buck Hunter Pro (arcade, 2006; designed by Play Mechanix, made and distributed by Raw Thrills)\",","     \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",","-    \"genre\": \"Arcade light-gun hunting shooter (a shooting gallery in a living landscape) with party versus and bonus mini-games\",","+    \"genre\": \"Arcade light-gun hunting shooter (a shooting gallery in a living landscape) with party versus, trophy encounters and bonus mini-games\",","     \"perspective\": \"First person on rails: a fixed vantage per site with scripted camera pans over a pseudo-3D heightfield landscape; a slow-motion Trophy Cam; side-on x-ray Shot Charts; 2D menus and an engine side-view Lodge\",","-    \"tech\": \"unknown\",","-    \"artDirection\": \"unknown\",","-    \"animation\": \"unknown\",","-    \"audio\": \"unknown\",","-    \"online\": \"unknown\",","-    \"testing\": \"unknown\",","-    \"research\": \"unknown\",","-    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",","+    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff package (full engine, lightly changed) plus about 4,800 lines of game code in vanilla JavaScript: an own software renderer on Canvas 2D (column-marched heightfield, depth buffer, shaded capsule pixel volumes), a procedural quadruped rig, Web Audio; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; tests on Node 24.22.1 and Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium (build 1243)\",","+    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's native retro-modern pixel style at 480x270 (E.tones shading with ordered dither, 1-pixel outlines, the 5x7 pixel font, E.font.title logos, E.ui windows, Humanoid portraits); new procedural deer, elk, moose, canids, the cow, critters, birds, antlers, trees, rocks, barn, blinds, canoe, scarecrow, snowmen and clays; three palettes: autumn morning, alpine dusk, first snow\",","+    \"animation\": \"Engine-native procedural animation posed by math every step: a new quadruped rig (walk, trot, gallop and bound gaits, graze, alert, look, call, hurt, limp, jump, death), small procedural critter and bird rigs (hops, flaps, peeks, struts), in-world capsule folk, and the engine's E.Humanoid and E.Blob in the Lodge and dialog portraits\",","+    \"audio\": \"All in code: bluegrass chiptune songs on the engine synth (title hoedown, lodge fire, stalking music with drum and tension layers, bonus jamboree, results, stings), layered sound effects (rifle crack with thump, tail and two valley echoes, pump, shells, calls, impacts, critters), ambience beds per hunt, and Animalese-style gibberish voices for six characters through formant filters\",","+    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1-4 players: the game's own card, a 3-minute Hub Hunt-Off keyed to the hub clock, ghost reticles and shots, progress every second, one result (also on time-up), round-over standings. The real harness passed with 2 players, with 4 players at latency 150 / jitter 50 / loss 5, and with host-leave\",","+    \"testing\": \"Allowed: unlimited headless testing with the engine's game.advance and game.debug, a scripted playthrough of the whole game, one command printing only failures and a count, screenshots only where scripts can't check, no subagent or workflow reviews. Ran: node tests/run.mjs, 210 headless checks in 7 suites (unit, sites, modes, playthrough of the whole Hunt-Off, attract/dev/saves/determinism, touch-only, AI Hub stub), all passing; --browser adds 22 Playwright checks (15 deep links with no errors, pick agreement, gamepad glyphs, the phone gate), all passing; the AI Hub harness in 3 scenarios, all passing; screenshots reviewed by eye\",","+    \"research\": \"None by the build stage beyond the plan's: the plan read Wikipedia's Big Buck Hunter article, the Highway Games cabinet listing and Macworld's iPhone review (other sites gave search summaries only); the build read the my-3D2dge handoff docs (README, API.md, the index) and the AI Hub lib/hub README and ghost example\",","+    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Playwright Chromium (headless shell, build 1243) for checks\",","     \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",","-    \"usage\": \"unknown\"","+    \"usage\": \"Cost and token totals: unknown (no meter available in the session); session time about 1 hour 15 minutes (05:05 to about 06:20)\"","   },","   \"testingQuestions\": [\"How many issues did testing catch?\", \"How many were critical / game breaking?\", \"Most helpful test\", \"Least helpful test\"],","-  \"testingFeedback\": [\"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\"],","+  \"testingFeedback\": [","+    \"About 30: a coroutine infinite loop on zero-length waits (Big Mo's site hung), a 30x slowdown from running the engine in a vm sandbox, an int hash deopt, the creek carved into a 6 m gorge, overlapping site fans burying a vantage in a hillside, moose wading 2.5 m deep, reeds and corn blocking shots, the bot leading hitscan shots and locking on hidden targets, dry cells marked as water, animals spawning far outside the view, touch-only not clearing, the hub sending no ghosts during the opening pan, glyph keycaps unreadable, a listener crash on shot events, the lodge exit and several test-timing issues\",","+    \"Five would have broken the game: the coroutine hang (a frozen trophy), the gorge and hillside terrain (unplayable sites), the moose underwater (unwinnable site) and the missing ghost messages (the hub would reject the game)\",","+    \"The scripted playthrough of the whole Hunt-Off with the cheat bot, together with the per-site bot runs: they exercised every site, trophy, bonus, tally and results screen and found the hang and the unwinnable sites\",","+    \"The determinism hash check: it passed first time and caught nothing, though it guards the hub sync\"","+  ],","   \"engineQuestions\": [\"What I liked most\", \"Stuck or guessed wrong\", \"Most important thing I built\", \"Hardest part\", \"What I changed in the engine, and why\", \"One thing I would change\"],","-  \"engineFeedback\": [\"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\"],","+  \"engineFeedback\": [","+    \"The standard features: the pause menu, settings, rebinding, controls screen, glyph families, full screen and boot screen came free, and E.Dialog with live Humanoid portraits gave the cast a voice in minutes. game.advance made fast headless tests easy\",","+    \"Yes: the pixel helpers cache the fill colour, and the font's default outline flooded small keycaps; I first guessed the cache was the cause. I also guessed that loading the engine in a vm sandbox was fine; global lookups there were 30x slower\",","+    \"The Vista renderer: a column-marched heightfield with a depth buffer and shaded capsule pixel volumes, so terrain, trees, animals and the scope lens share one depth test, and shots hit exactly what is drawn\",","+    \"Fitting a first-person, perspective game into an engine whose views are orthographic: none of the world drawing (props, lights, particles, the camera) could be reused for the hunt itself, only the HUD, menus and the Lodge\",","+    \"Three small changes: the default button symbols are PlayStation (TASK.md asks for them; the Xbox option stays); audio.bus('sfx' | 'music') returns the bus node so the gibberish voices follow the effects volume and mute; the Input's default glyph family matches. Everything else lives in the game's own modules\",","+    \"A perspective (first-person or chase) view with a depth buffer in the 2D engine, so props, rigs and lights could be drawn into it\"","+  ],","   \"promptQuestions\": [\"What I liked most\", \"What was confusing\", \"Hardest thing to do\", \"What I would change\"],","-  \"promptFeedback\": [\"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\"],","-  \"credits\": [[\"Game\", \"Big Buck Hunt-Off, an original game inspired by Big Buck Hunter Pro\"], [\"Engine\", \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 by Michael Crosato (MIT)\"], [\"Online\", \"AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (Session Protocol v1)\"], [\"Sound\", \"All music, sound effects and voices synthesized in code\"], [\"Cast\", \"The Emcee, Uncle Dub, Granny Mae, Cousin Dwayne, Loretta Pruitt, Big Earl, Hank the scarecrow, Bessie\"]],","+  \"promptFeedback\": [","+    \"A concrete plan to build from plus a clear definition of done, with testing rules that say exactly how to prove it works\",","+    \"The plan names a dev folder and file with 'max' and yesterday's timestamp, while TASK.md names 'medium' and today's; TASK.md wins, as STAGE.md says, but it took a moment to be sure\",","+    \"Getting a whole feature-complete arcade game (renderer, rigs, nine sites, three trophies, three bonus games, a range, party, attract, dev mode, AI Hub) built and verified in one session\",","+    \"Let the plan's file names be filled in by the build stage, and say up front how large a plan is (1,560 lines) so the build can budget its reading\"","+  ],","+  \"credits\": [[\"Game\", \"Big Buck Hunt-Off, an original game inspired by Big Buck Hunter Pro. No names, art, music or levels from the source\"], [\"Engine\", \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 by Michael Crosato (MIT), with a small change list in Engine Feedback\"], [\"Online\", \"AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (Session Protocol v1)\"], [\"Sound\", \"All music, sound effects and voices synthesized in code\"], [\"Cast\", \"The Emcee, Uncle Dub, Granny Mae, Cousin Dwayne, Loretta Pruitt, Big Earl, Hank the scarecrow, Bessie the cow\"], [\"Built by\", \"Anthropic claude-opus-5-5 (medium effort) in Claude Code, from PLAN.md\"]],","   \"aiHub\": {","     \"name\": \"Big Buck Hunt-Off\",","     \"tagline\": \"Bucks only. Bragging rights forever.\","]}],"originalFile":"{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:05:54\",\n    \"source\": \"Big Buck Hunter Pro (arcade, 2006; designed by Play Mechanix, made and distributed by Raw Thrills)\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Arcade light-gun hunting shooter (a shooting gallery in a living landscape) with party versus and bonus mini-games\",\n    \"perspective\": \"First person on rails: a fixed vantage per site with scripted camera pans over a pseudo-3D heightfield landscape; a slow-motion Trophy Cam; side-on x-ray Shot Charts; 2D menus and an engine side-view Lodge\",\n    \"tech\": \"unknown\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"unknown\",\n    \"animation\": \"unknown\",\n    \"audio\": \"unknown\",\n    \"online\": \"unknown\",\n    \"testing\": \"unknown\",\n    \"research\": \"unknown\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"unknown\"\n  },\n  \"testingQuestions\": [\"How many issues did testing catch?\", \"How many were critical / game breaking?\", \"Most helpful test\", \"Least helpful test\"],\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\"],\n  \"engineQuestions\": [\"What I liked most\", \"Stuck or guessed wrong\", \"Most important thing I built\", \"Hardest part\", \"What I changed in the engine, and why\", \"One thing I would change\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\"],\n  \"promptQuestions\": [\"What I liked most\", \"What was confusing\", \"Hardest thing to do\", \"What I would change\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\"],\n  \"credits\": [[\"Game\", \"Big Buck Hunt-Off, an original game inspired by Big Buck Hunter Pro\"], [\"Engine\", \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 by Michael Crosato (MIT)\"], [\"Online\", \"AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (Session Protocol v1)\"], [\"Sound\", \"All music, sound effects and voices synthesized in code\"], [\"Cast\", \"The Emcee, Uncle Dub, Granny Mae, Cousin Dwayne, Loretta Pruitt, Big Earl, Hank the scarecrow, Bessie\"]],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Big Buck Hunt-Off\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Bucks only. Bragging rights forever.\",\n    \"description\": \"An arcade light-gun hunting shooter in living pixel landscapes: bag the bucks, spare the does, and win the Hunt-Off alone, on the couch or online.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Shooter\",\n    \"source\": \"Big Buck Hunter Pro\",\n    \"series\": \"Big Buck Hunter\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Aim: mouse or left stick · Shoot: left click or R2 · Pump: R or Square · Scope: right click or L2 · Call: Q or Triangle\",\n    \"tags\": [\"first-person\", \"arcade\", \"pixel art\", \"versus\", \"comedy\", \"retro\"]\n  }\n}\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VmeDPi5mtY1MwChdbTHYxY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
