{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The transcript shows the bundled single .html file exists in the folder root and exit-interview.json parses with no 'unknown' values, and the final reply contains all four required sections. But the condition also requires every TASK.md feature to be implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, and the transcript does not establish that. Several TASK.md items are not demonstrated in full: the Engine Feedback item 'what did you change in the engine' lists an audio bus addition the transcript only partly tests, the Lodge's engine portrait and Blob use is only checked for draw calls, the dev-mode tools were checked after a late edit, and some TASK.md items (for example the Animal Lab 'every item' and the 'every site reviewed by eye' claim) are asserted in the summary but not fully shown. The final reply also states testing coverage ('every mode played to the end', 'every item') beyond what the transcript records item by item. Because the requirement that every feature be demonstrably implemented is not clearly met from transcript evidence alone, the condition is not satisfied."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3fa61e8-1431-4900-ae89-edc59162574b","uuid":"fac9dee2-675a-4b88-ab4a-d396ecacb519","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:03:31.576Z","isSynthetic":true}
