{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundle, exit-interview.json (parses, no 'unknown' values) and the four report sections are all present, and the test and AI Hub harness evidence is strong. But the condition requires every TASK.md feature to be demonstrably implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, and the transcript does not establish that across the full scope. Several requirements rest on summaries rather than item-level records: the 'every site reviewed by eye' claim (earlier site views were partial), 'every mode played to the end', 'every item', and 'every dev tool'. The Lodge's Humanoid and Blob rigs are supported by pixel counts, draw calls and screenshots rather than a full visual review. The last assistant message declined to run further checks and reworded the report instead, so these gaps remain open."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3fa61e8-1431-4900-ae89-edc59162574b","uuid":"c44142a6-5d5c-4f88-b090-e5c779b67f8f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:49:55.246Z","isSynthetic":true}
